her Alex and AP-5 have low, medium, or high respon...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Alex"},"2":{"Display":"AP-5"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2"],"Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"All"},"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"Answers":{"1":{"Display":"Low Responsibility"},"2":{"Display":"Medium Responsibility"},"3":{"Display":"High Responsibility"}},"AnswerOrder":["1","2","3"],"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","TextPosition":"inline","RepeatHeaders":"none","WhiteSpace":"OFF","MobileFirst":true},"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":4,"ChoiceDataExportTags":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID171","SecondaryAttribute":"Evaluation Task \u00a0 Your task is to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have low, medium, or high respon..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center; width: 875px;\"><u><strong>Evaluation Task<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify; width: 875px;\">Your task is to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have <em><strong>low<\/strong><\/em>, <em><strong>medium<\/strong><\/em>, or <em><strong>high<\/strong><\/em> responsibility for their team losing the game.<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\">\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Consider the game in the left figure where Team A lost, and the counterfactual game in the right figure which shows what would have happened had Alex played <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round #3<\/strong>. Once you understand what happened in the two games, <strong>please answer the question below<\/strong>.<\/div>\n<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td>\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Original game<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_u0Ztbz2MTz5qNN0\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 438px;\" width=\"350\" \/>&nbsp;<\/div>\n<\/td>\n<td>\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_vZHyPw6QPg6Gt0Y\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 438px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/div>\n<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><br \/>\nRemember, while we can see all the cards,&nbsp;<strong>the players do not see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>.<br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify; width: 875px;\">To what extent do you think Alex and AP-5 are responsible for their team losing the game? Please indicate the degree of their responsibility by selecting the appropriate choice below:<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n","DataExportTag":"CF-A0-P-B1-TRxCH-215","QuestionID":"QID171","QuestionType":"Matrix","Selector":"Likert","SubSelector":"SingleAnswer","QuestionDescription":"Evaluation Task \u00a0 Your task is to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have low, medium, or high respon...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Alex"},"2":{"Display":"AP-5"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2"],"Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"All"},"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"Answers":{"1":{"Display":"Low Responsibility"},"2":{"Display":"Medium Responsibility"},"3":{"Display":"High Responsibility"}},"AnswerOrder":["1","2","3"],"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","TextPosition":"inline","RepeatHeaders":"none","WhiteSpace":"OFF","MobileFirst":true},"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":4,"ChoiceDataExportTags":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719","SecondaryAttribute":"Evaluation Task Your task is to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have low, medium, or high responsi...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center; width: 875px;\"><u><strong>Evaluation Task<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify; width: 875px;\"><br \/>\nYour task is to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have <strong><em>low<\/em><\/strong>, <em><strong>medium<\/strong><\/em>, or <em><strong>high<\/strong><\/em> responsibility for their team losing the game.&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>\n<div style=\"text-align: justify; width: 875px;\">Consider the following game where <strong>Team A lost<\/strong>. Once you understand what happened in the game, <strong>please answer the question below<\/strong>.&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center; width: 875px;\">&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_Rr3oOxCJRF2FtMd\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center; width: 875px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center; width: 875px;\">Remember,&nbsp;<strong>the players see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center; width: 875px;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify; width: 875px;\">To what extent do you think Alex and AP-5 are responsible for their team losing the game? Please indicate the&nbsp;degree of their responsibility by selecting the appropriate choice below:<\/div>\n\n<table>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n\n","DataExportTag":"Q1719","QuestionType":"Matrix","Selector":"Likert","SubSelector":"SingleAnswer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","TextPosition":"inline","RepeatHeaders":"none","WhiteSpace":"OFF","MobileFirst":true},"QuestionDescription":"Evaluation Task Your task is to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have low, medium, or high responsi...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Alex"},"2":{"Display":"AP-5"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2"],"Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"All"},"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":4,"Answers":{"1":{"Display":"Low Responsibility"},"2":{"Display":"Medium Responsibility"},"3":{"Display":"High Responsibility"}},"AnswerOrder":["1","2","3"],"ChoiceDataExportTags":false,"QuestionID":"QID1719"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345396","SecondaryAttribute":"Consent Form \u00a0 What is the purpose of this research project? In this research project, we are stu..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><span style=\"font-size:24px;\"><strong>Consent Form<\/strong><\/span><\/u><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br>\n&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><u><strong>What is the purpose of this research project?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nIn this research project, we are studying the design of trustworthy AI systems with multiple agents that interact over time. Crucial aspects of trustworthy AI that we want to investigate in this research project are related to accountable decision making, and include agent designs that can provide explanations (justifications) for their decisions, and system designs that can infer the actual causes of outcomes and attribute responsibility (blame) for these outcomes.<br>\n<br>\nIn this study, we will ask respondents to disclose how they think they would attribute responsibility (blame) for the decision outcomes to the agents.<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>How long will the study last?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nWe expect that the study will take you between 20 and 25 minutes to complete. The participation is voluntary and you are free to leave the experiment at any time you like by simply closing the web browser.<br> \n<br>\n<u><strong>What will I need to do in this study?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nIn this study, you will be asked to answer a series of questions about the decisions of a system. After observing the system's decisions, you will be asked to disclose how you think you would attribute responsibility (blame) for the decision outcomes to the agents.<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>Is there any way being in this study could be bad for me?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nWe don\u2019t believe that there are any risks from participating in this research beyond those encountered in every day computer use.<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>Will being in this study help me in any way?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nWe cannot promise any direct benefits to you from taking part in this study, but we hope that this research will enable us to get a better understanding of people\u2019s perceptions of AI systems.<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>Please note that:<\/strong><\/u><br>\n\u2022 Whether or not you take part is up to you.<br>\n\u2022 Your participation is completely voluntary.<br>\n\u2022 You can choose not to take part.<br>\n\u2022 You can agree to take part and later change your mind.<br>\n\u2022 Your decision will not be held against you.<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>If I take part in this research, how will my privacy be protected? What happens to the information you collect?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nTo protect your privacy, we will not collect any personally identifiable information. The study data will be stored on secure password protected servers at MPI-SWS. Your Prolific worker identifiers will be deleted from our database immediately after paying you for participating in the experiment. Anonymized data, not containing your identifiers, will be stored and potentially shared publicly, to promote reproducibility of research.<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>How will I be compensated for my time?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nIf you agree to take part in this research study, we will pay you \u00a32.54 for your time and effort.<br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp;<br>\n<u><strong>Who can I talk to if I have any questions?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nIf you have any questions, concerns, or complaints, please feel free to contact the research team led by Goran Radanovi\u0107, who can be reached at Campus E1 5, 66123 Saarbr\u00fccken, Germany, gradanovic@mpi-sws.org.<br>\nThis research has been reviewed and approved by the ethical review board of the faculty of Mathematics and Computer Science at Saarland University. If<br>\n\u2022 Your questions, concerns, or complaints are not being answered by the research team.<br>\n\u2022 You cannot reach the research team.<br>\n\u2022 You want to talk to someone besides the research team.<br>\n\u2022 You have questions about your rights as a research subject.<br>\n\u2022 You want to get information or provide input about this research.<br>\n<br>\nYou may contact the ethical review board of the faculty of Mathematics and Computer Science at Saarland University (https:\/\/erb.cs.uni-saarland.de).<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>Please respond to the questions below<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n<br>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Consent Form \u00a0 What is the purpose of this research project? In this research project, we are stu...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><span style=\"font-size:24px;\"><strong>Consent Form<\/strong><\/span><\/u><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br>\n&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><u><strong>What is the purpose of this research project?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nIn this research project, we are studying the design of trustworthy AI systems with multiple agents that interact over time. Crucial aspects of trustworthy AI that we want to investigate in this research project are related to accountable decision making, and include agent designs that can provide explanations (justifications) for their decisions, and system designs that can infer the actual causes of outcomes and attribute responsibility (blame) for these outcomes.<br>\n<br>\nIn this study, we will ask respondents to disclose how they think they would attribute responsibility (blame) for the decision outcomes to the agents.<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>How long will the study last?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nWe expect that the study will take you between [X] and [Y] minutes to complete. The participation is voluntary and you are free to leave the experiment at any time you like by simply closing the web browser.<br> \n<br>\n<u><strong>What will I need to do in this study?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nIn this study, you will be asked to answer a series of questions about the decisions of a system. After observing the system's decisions, you will be asked to disclose how you think you would attribute responsibility (blame) for the decision outcomes to the agents.<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>Is there any way being in this study could be bad for me?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nWe don\u2019t believe that there are any risks from participating in this research beyond those encountered in every day computer use.<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>Will being in this study help me in any way?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nWe cannot promise any direct benefits to you from taking part in this study, but we hope that this research will enable us to get a better understanding of people\u2019s perceptions of AI systems.<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>Please note that:<\/strong><\/u><br>\n\u2022 Whether or not you take part is up to you.<br>\n\u2022 Your participation is completely voluntary.<br>\n\u2022 You can choose not to take part.<br>\n\u2022 You can agree to take part and later change your mind.<br>\n\u2022 Your decision will not be held against you.<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>If I take part in this research, how will my privacy be protected? What happens to the information you collect?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nTo protect your privacy, we will not collect any personally identifiable information. The study data will be stored on secure password protected servers at MPI-SWS. Your [Prolific\/AMT] worker identifiers will be deleted from our database immediately after paying you for participating in the experiment. Anonymized data, not containing your identifiers, will be stored and potentially shared publicly, to promote reproducibility of research.<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>How will I be compensated for my time?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nIf you agree to take part in this research study, we will pay you $[X] for your time and effort.<br>\n&nbsp; &nbsp;<br>\n<u><strong>Who can I talk to if I have any questions?<\/strong><\/u><br>\nIf you have any questions, concerns, or complaints, please feel free to contact the research team led by Goran Radanovi\u0107, who can be reached at Campus E1 5, 66123 Saarbr\u00fccken, Germany, gradanovic@mpi-sws.org.<br>\nThis research has been reviewed and approved by the ethical review board of the faculty of Mathematics and Computer Science at Saarland University. If<br>\n\u2022 Your questions, concerns, or complaints are not being answered by the research team.<br>\n\u2022 You cannot reach the research team.<br>\n\u2022 You want to talk to someone besides the research team.<br>\n\u2022 You have questions about your rights as a research subject.<br>\n\u2022 You want to get information or provide input about this research.<br>\n<br>\nYou may contact the ethical review board of the faculty of Mathematics and Computer Science at Saarland University (https:\/\/erb.cs.uni-saarland.de).<br>\n<br>\n<u><strong>Please respond to the questions below<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n<br>","DataExportTag":"ERB-Q1","QuestionID":"QID1719345396"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345397","SecondaryAttribute":"I am 18 years of age or older.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"I am 18 years of age or older.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"I am 18 years of age or older.","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Yes"},"2":{"Display":"No"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345397\/SelectableChoice\/1","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">I am 18 years of age or older.<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Yes<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345397\/SelectableChoice\/1","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345397","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345397","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"MinimumAge","libraryID":"UR_RlLMb9WtlAwpgoj","messageID":"MS_M4LLoQW5XOiMpVY","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"I am 18 years of age or older.","DataExportTag":"ERB-Q2","QuestionID":"QID1719345397"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345398","SecondaryAttribute":"I have read this consent form in its entirety or had it read to me.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"I have read this consent form in its entirety or had it read to me.","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"I have read this consent form in its entirety or had it read to me.","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Yes"},"2":{"Display":"No"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345398\/SelectableChoice\/1","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">I have read this consent form in its entirety or had it read to me.<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Yes<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345398\/SelectableChoice\/1","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345398","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345398","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"ReadAll","libraryID":"UR_RlLMb9WtlAwpgoj","messageID":"MS_kLWvgmiMVKTSFz2","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":1,"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"I have read this consent form in its entirety or had it read to me.","DataExportTag":"ERB-Q3","QuestionID":"QID1719345398"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345399","SecondaryAttribute":"I voluntarily consent to participate in this research. ","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"I voluntarily consent to participate in this research. &nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","Autoscale":{"YScale":{"Name":"yesNo","Type":"likert","Reverse":true}}},"QuestionDescription":"I voluntarily consent to participate in this research. ","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Yes"},"2":{"Display":"No"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345399\/SelectableChoice\/1","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">I voluntarily consent to participate in this research. <\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Yes<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345399\/SelectableChoice\/1","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345399","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345399","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"ConsentValidation","libraryID":"UR_RlLMb9WtlAwpgoj","messageID":"MS_jqKs0Bmu1t5aFwh","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":1,"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"I voluntarily consent to participate in this research. &nbsp;","DataExportTag":"ERB-Q4","QuestionID":"QID1719345399"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345400","SecondaryAttribute":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTask Description \u00a0 In this study, you will be asked a series of questions about a te","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<u><strong>Task Description<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this study, you will be asked a series of questions about a team-based card game. Specifically, you will be asked to evaluate the <em><strong>degree of responsibility<\/strong><\/em> exhibited by each player in a team that <strong><em>lost<\/em> <\/strong>in a card game.&nbsp;<br \/>\n<br \/>\nFor this purpose, we will consider a team-based variant of the Goofspiel card game, where two teams, Team A and Team B, compete against each other. Each team consists of a human player and an AI bot.<strong><em> Alex<\/em> <em>(human)<\/em><\/strong><em> <\/em>and <strong><em>AP-5 (AI)<\/em><\/strong><em><strong> <\/strong><\/em>play in <strong><em>Team A<\/em><\/strong>, while <strong><em>Billie<\/em><\/strong> <em><strong>(human) <\/strong><\/em>and <strong><em>BB-8<\/em><\/strong> <em><strong>(AI)<\/strong><\/em> play in <strong><em>Team B<\/em><\/strong>.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nWe will first ask you to complete a <em><strong>tutorial<\/strong><\/em>. This tutorial will have three parts:<\/div>\n\n<ol>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Goofspiel<\/em>: this part explains the rules of the Goofspiel card game.<\/li>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/em>: this part explains counterfactual reasoning in Goofspiel.&nbsp;<\/li>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Evaluation Task<\/em>: this part provides an example of evaluation tasks that you will be asked to solve.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br \/>\nAfter completing the tutorial, you will be asked to evaluate 5 games. We will show you 5 Goofspiel games <em><strong>where Team A lost<\/strong><\/em>, and your task is to evaluate to what extent Alex and AP-5 are responsible for this outcome, that is, assess whether they have <strong><em>low<\/em><\/strong>, <strong><em>medium<\/em><\/strong>, or <strong><em>high<\/em><\/strong><strong> <\/strong>responsibility for Team A losing the game.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<em>Please note that all the games that you will see are illustrative examples, and they were not played by actual human-AI teams.<\/em><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"margin-left: 40px;\"><br type=\"_moz\" \/>\n&nbsp;<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTask Description \u00a0 In this study, you will be asked a series of questions about a team-based...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<u><strong>Task Description<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this study, you will be asked a series of questions about a team-based card game. Specifically, you will be asked to evaluate the <em><strong>degree of responsibility<\/strong><\/em> exhibited by each player in a team that <strong><em>lost<\/em> <\/strong>in a card game.&nbsp;<br \/>\n<br \/>\nFor this purpose, we will consider a team-based variant of the Goofspiel card game, where two teams, Team A and Team B, compete against each other. Each team consists of a human player and an AI bot.<strong><em> Alex<\/em> <em>(human)<\/em><\/strong><em> <\/em>and <strong><em>AP-5 (AI)<\/em><\/strong><em><strong> <\/strong><\/em>play in <strong><em>Team A<\/em><\/strong>, while <strong><em>Billie<\/em><\/strong> <em><strong>(human) <\/strong><\/em>and <strong><em>BB-8<\/em><\/strong> <em><strong>(AI)<\/strong><\/em> play in <strong><em>Team B<\/em><\/strong>.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nWe will first ask you to complete a <em><strong>tutorial<\/strong><\/em>. This tutorial will have three parts:<\/div>\n\n<ol>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Goofspiel<\/em>: this part explains the rules of the Goofspiel card game.<\/li>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/em>: this part explains counterfactual reasoning in Goofspiel.&nbsp;<\/li>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Evaluation Task<\/em>: this part provides an example of evaluation tasks that you will be asked to solve.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br \/>\nAfter completing the tutorial, you will be asked to evaluate 5 games. We will show you 5 Goofspiel games <em><strong>where Team A lost<\/strong><\/em>, and your task is to evaluate to what extent Alex and AP-5 are responsible for this outcome, that is, assess whether they have <strong><em>low<\/em><\/strong>, <strong><em>medium<\/em><\/strong>, or <strong><em>high<\/em><\/strong><strong> <\/strong>responsibility for Team A losing the game.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<em>Please note that all the games that you will see are illustrative examples, and they were not played by actual human-AI teams.<\/em><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"margin-left: 40px;\"><br type=\"_moz\" \/>\n&nbsp;<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q1","QuestionID":"QID1719345400"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345401","SecondaryAttribute":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTutorial - Goofspiel \u00a0 To solve your tasks, you need to familiarize yourself with th","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<u><strong>Tutorial - Goofspiel<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">To solve your tasks, you need to familiarize yourself with the rules of the team-based version of Goofspiel. The rules are as follows:<\/div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the beginning of the game, each player receives 5 cards from the standard 52 card deck&nbsp;-&nbsp;<strong>players do not see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>, but they are aware that any given player holds cards of only one suit. Additionally, a separate deck of cards is shuffled, called <em>prize deck<\/em>.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The game proceeds in <em>rounds<\/em>. In each round, one prize card is drawn from the prize deck, and upon observing&nbsp;the prize&nbsp;card,&nbsp;the&nbsp;players simultaneously select one card from their hand. The team that plays cards with a higher sum&nbsp;wins the prize card, and the&nbsp;prize is added to the team&#39;s score. If&nbsp;the teams have equal sums, the prize card is discarded and the scores remain the same.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The game finishes after round #5, and the team with&nbsp;the highest score wins. If the teams have equal score, then it&#39;s a draw.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<div>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" height=\"630\" width=\"723\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Example 1<\/strong>: We explain how games are represented using the game below.&nbsp;The&nbsp;<em>rounds <\/em>are<em> <\/em>represented as circles: the first round (round #1) is&nbsp;on the outermost circle, while the last round (round #5)&nbsp;is on the innermost circle. The cards that players played in the game are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">grey boxes<\/span><\/span>. The prize cards are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">yellow boxes<\/span><\/span>.\n\n\t\t\t<div>players played in the game are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">grey boxes<\/span><\/span>. The prize cards are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">yellow boxes<\/span><\/span>.<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_gbgxxk3wwIVyDME\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this example, all players initially received&nbsp;cards 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7 (round #1). Note that in general players do not have to receive the same cards. In the first round (round #1), <span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">prize card&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;was drawn from the prize deck,&nbsp;<\/span>both Alex and AP-5 played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/strong>, Billie played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>, and BB-8 <span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">played card <\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">.&nbsp;<\/span>Team B won the prize card&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/strong>: Team A played cards whose sum is 6, and Team B played cards whose sum is 9.<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\tTeam A won the prize cards in round #2 and round #4, achieving the score of <strong><span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><span style=\"background-color:#420516;\">11<\/span><\/span><\/strong>. Team B won all the other prizes, achieving the score of <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#420516;\">14<\/span><\/strong><\/span>. Hence, Team B won the game, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#420516;\"><strong>red scoreboard<\/strong><\/span>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><br \/>\nNow that you are familiar with the rules of Goofspiel and the game representation, we ask you to answer the questions below.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTutorial - Goofspiel \u00a0 To solve your tasks, you need to familiarize yourself with the rules...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<u><strong>Tutorial - Goofspiel<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">To solve your tasks, you need to familiarize yourself with the rules of the team-based version of Goofspiel. The rules are as follows:<\/div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the beginning of the game, each player receives 5 cards from the standard 52 card deck&nbsp;-&nbsp;<strong>players do not see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>, but they are aware that any given player holds cards of only one suit. Additionally, a separate deck of cards is shuffled, called <em>prize deck<\/em>.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The game proceeds in <em>rounds<\/em>. In each round, one prize card is drawn from the prize deck, and upon observing&nbsp;the prize&nbsp;card,&nbsp;the&nbsp;players simultaneously select one card from their hand. The team that plays cards with a higher sum&nbsp;wins the prize card, and the&nbsp;prize is added to the team&#39;s score. If&nbsp;the teams have equal sums, the prize card is discarded and the scores remain the same.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The game finishes after round #5, and the team with&nbsp;the highest score wins. If the teams have equal score, then it&#39;s a draw.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<div>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" height=\"630\" width=\"723\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Example 1<\/strong>: We explain how games are represented using the game below.&nbsp;The&nbsp;<em>rounds <\/em>are<em> <\/em>represented as circles: the first round (round #1) is&nbsp;on the outermost circle, while the last round (round #5)&nbsp;is on the innermost circle. The cards that players played in the game are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">grey boxes<\/span><\/span>. The prize cards are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">yellow boxes<\/span><\/span>.<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_2Bo95zy0fCWG473\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this example, all players initially received&nbsp;cards 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7 (round #1). Note that in general players do not have to receive the same cards. In the first round (round #1), <span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">prize card&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;was drawn from the prize deck,&nbsp;<\/span>both Alex and AP-5 played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/strong>, Billie played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>, and BB-8 <span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">played card <\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">.&nbsp;<\/span>Team B won the prize card&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/strong>: Team A played cards whose sum is 6, and Team B played cards whose sum is 9.<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\tTeam A won the prize cards in round #2 and round #4, achieving the score of <strong><span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><span style=\"background-color:#420516;\">11<\/span><\/span><\/strong>. Team B won all the other prizes, achieving the score of <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#420516;\">14<\/span><\/strong><\/span>. Hence, Team B won the game, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#420516;\"><strong>red scoreboard<\/strong><\/span>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><br \/>\nNow that you are familiar with the rules of Goofspiel and the game representation, we ask you to answer the questions below.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/p>","DataExportTag":"Q2","QuestionID":"QID1719345401"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345402","SecondaryAttribute":"In Example 1, what card did AP-5 play in round #2?\u00a0","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In Example 1, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #2<\/strong>?&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In Example 1, what card did AP-5 play in round #2?\u00a0","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"3"},"5":{"Display":"4"},"6":{"Display":"5"},"7":{"Display":"6"},"10":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","10"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345402\/SelectableChoice\/10","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In Example 1, what card did AP-5 play in round #2?&nbsp;<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">7<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345402\/SelectableChoice\/10","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345402","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345402","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":13,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In Example 1, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #2<\/strong>?&nbsp;","DataExportTag":"Q3","QuestionID":"QID1719345402"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345403","SecondaryAttribute":"In Example 1, what was the prize in round #3?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In Example 1, what was the prize in <strong>round #3<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In Example 1, what was the prize in round #3?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"3"},"5":{"Display":"4"},"6":{"Display":"5"},"7":{"Display":"6"},"8":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345403\/SelectableChoice\/8","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In Example 1, what was the prize in round #3?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">7<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345403\/SelectableChoice\/8","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345403","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345403","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":10,"NextAnswerId":1,"SubSelector":"TX","QuestionText_Unsafe":"In Example 1, what was the prize in <strong>round #3<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q4","QuestionID":"QID1719345403"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345404","SecondaryAttribute":"In Example 1, which team won the prize in round #4?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In Example 1, which team won the prize in <strong>round #4<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In Example 1, which team won the prize in round #4?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"Team A"},"5":{"Display":"Team B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5"],"Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"All"},"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345404\/SelectableChoice\/4","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In Example 1, which team won the prize in round #4?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Team A<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345404\/SelectableChoice\/4","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345404","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345404","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":7,"NextAnswerId":5,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In Example 1, which team won the prize in <strong>round #4<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q5","QuestionID":"QID1719345404"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345405","SecondaryAttribute":"Tutorial - Counterfactuals \u00a0\u00a0 To solve your tasks, you also need to familiarize yourself with cou.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"display: block;&gt;\n\n&lt;p style=\">\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">To solve your tasks, you also need to familiarize yourself with <em>counterfactuals<\/em>.&nbsp;In this task, <em><strong>counterfactual games<\/strong><\/em> show what would have happened had the players played their cards differently. We continue with the previous example to explain counterfactual games.<\/p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 1 (continued)<\/strong>: We have seen that in this example Team A lost (<em>the left figure below<\/em>). However, consider the following question:&nbsp;<span style=\"text-align: center;\"> <\/span><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>What would have happened had AP-5 played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> in<\/em><em><strong> round #2<\/strong>?<\/em><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Clearly, nothing would have changed in <em>round #1<\/em>. However, the <strong>cards<\/strong> the players would have played in <strong>round&nbsp;#3<\/strong>, <strong>round #4<\/strong>, and <strong>round #5<\/strong>, can be <strong>different from<\/strong> those that are originally played. The <strong>right figure<\/strong> below shows the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>. The differences compared to the original game in the left figure are:<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #2<\/em>, we imagine that AP-5 had played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> instead of card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">7<\/span><\/span><\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round&nbsp;#3<\/em>, <em>round #4<\/em>, and <em>round&nbsp;#5<\/em>, we imagine that all the players had responded to this change and had played cards in<strong> <\/strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ffb38a;\">light orange<\/span><\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#d55e00;\"> <\/span><\/strong>boxes<span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><strong> <\/strong><\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Team A wins the counterfactual game, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#009e73;\">green scoreboard<\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ul>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 1&nbsp; &nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_2Bo95zy0fCWG473\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5 played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span> in round #2)<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_dV6DprmriLkQHjO\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n\n<div style=\"width: 100%; text-align: justify;\"><br \/>\nNow that you are familiar with counterfactuals games, we ask you to take a look at <em>another example<\/em>, and answer the questions below.&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 2<\/strong>: Please take a look at another game below, and one of its counterfactual games. Once you understand what happened in the counterfactual game, <strong>please answer the questions below<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 2<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_4E76y7AKw82EDb4\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had&nbsp;AP-5&nbsp;played <\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><span style=\"text-align: center;\"> in round #1)<\/span><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_OAVahJzEB5tNrAV\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Tutorial - Counterfactuals \u00a0\u00a0 To solve your tasks, you also need to familiarize yourself with cou...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"display: block;&gt;\n\n&lt;p style=\">\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">To solve your tasks, you also need to familiarize yourself with <em>counterfactuals<\/em>.&nbsp;In this task, <em><strong>counterfactual games<\/strong><\/em> show what would have happened had the players played their cards differently. We continue with the previous example to explain counterfactual games.<\/p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 1 (continued)<\/strong>: We have seen that in this example Team A lost (<em>the left figure below<\/em>). However, consider the following question:&nbsp;<span style=\"text-align: center;\"> <\/span><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>What would have happened had AP-5 played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> in<\/em><em><strong> round #2<\/strong>?<\/em><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Clearly, nothing would have changed in <em>round #1<\/em>. However, the <strong>cards<\/strong> the players would have played in <strong>round&nbsp;#3<\/strong>, <strong>round #4<\/strong>, and <strong>round #5<\/strong>, can be <strong>different from<\/strong> those that are originally played. The <strong>right figure<\/strong> below shows the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>. The differences compared to the original game in the left figure are:<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #2<\/em>, we imagine that AP-5 had played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> instead of card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">7<\/span><\/span><\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round&nbsp;#3<\/em>, <em>round #4<\/em>, and <em>round&nbsp;#5<\/em>, we imagine that all the players had responded to this change and had played cards in<strong> <\/strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ffb38a;\">light orange<\/span><\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#d55e00;\"> <\/span><\/strong>boxes<span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><strong> <\/strong><\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Team A wins the counterfactual game, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#009e73;\">green scoreboard<\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ul>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 1&nbsp; &nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_2Bo95zy0fCWG473\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5 played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span> in round #2)<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_dV6DprmriLkQHjO\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n\n<div style=\"width: 100%; text-align: justify;\"><br \/>\nNow that you are familiar with counterfactuals games, we ask you to take a look at <em>another example<\/em>, and answer the questions below.&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 2<\/strong>: Please take a look at another game below, and one of its counterfactual games. Once you understand what happened in the counterfactual game, <strong>please answer the questions below<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 2<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_4E76y7AKw82EDb4\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had&nbsp;AP-5&nbsp;played <\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><span style=\"text-align: center;\"> in round #1)<\/span><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_OAVahJzEB5tNrAV\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q6","QuestionID":"QID1719345405"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345406","SecondaryAttribute":"In the counterfactual game\u00a0in Example 2, what card did AP-5\u00a0play in round #1?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>&nbsp;in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong>&nbsp;play in <strong>round #1<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In the counterfactual game\u00a0in Example 2, what card did AP-5\u00a0play in round #1?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"3"},"5":{"Display":"4"},"6":{"Display":"5"},"7":{"Display":"6"},"8":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345406\/SelectableChoice\/5","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In the counterfactual game&amp;nbsp;in Example 2, what card did AP-5&amp;nbsp;play in round #1?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">4<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345406\/SelectableChoice\/5","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345406","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345406","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":10,"NextAnswerId":3,"SubSelector":"TX","QuestionText_Unsafe":"In the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>&nbsp;in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong>&nbsp;play in <strong>round #1<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q7","QuestionID":"QID1719345406"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345407","SecondaryAttribute":"In the counterfactual game\u00a0in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #4?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>&nbsp;in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #4<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In the counterfactual game\u00a0in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #4?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"3"},"5":{"Display":"4"},"6":{"Display":"5"},"7":{"Display":"6"},"8":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345407\/SelectableChoice\/8","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In the counterfactual game&amp;nbsp;in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #4?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">7<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345407\/SelectableChoice\/8","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345407","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345407","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":10,"NextAnswerId":3,"SubSelector":"TX","QuestionText_Unsafe":"In the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>&nbsp;in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #4<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q8","QuestionID":"QID1719345407"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345408","SecondaryAttribute":"Which team won in the counterfactual game in Example 2?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Which team won in the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong> in Example 2?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which team won in the counterfactual game in Example 2?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"Team A"},"5":{"Display":"Team B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345408\/SelectableChoice\/5","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Which team won in the counterfactual game in Example 2?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Team B<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345408\/SelectableChoice\/5","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345408","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345408","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":7,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Which team won in the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong> in Example 2?","DataExportTag":"Q9","QuestionID":"QID1719345408"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345409","SecondaryAttribute":"Tutorial - Counterfactuals \u00a0 Counterfactual games can be based on more complex scenarios. We cont..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/strong><\/u><\/p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Counterfactual games can be based on more complex scenarios. We continue with the previous example to demonstrate this.<\/p>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:1050px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"3\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 2 (continued)<\/strong>:&nbsp;We have seen that in this example&nbsp;Team A would not have won had AP-5 played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round 1&nbsp;<\/strong>(<em>the middle figure below<\/em>). However, we can also ask:<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>What would have happened had AP-5&nbsp;played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> in <\/em><em><strong>round #1<\/strong>&nbsp;and had Alex&nbsp;played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> <\/em><em>in <strong>r<\/strong><\/em><strong>ound #2<\/strong><em>?<\/em><\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><br \/>\n\t\t\tThis yields a <strong>new counterfactual <\/strong>game depicted in the <strong>right figure<\/strong> below. The differences compared to the <em>previous&nbsp;counterfactual game<\/em> in the middle&nbsp;figure are:<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #2<\/em>, we imagine that Alex had played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> instead of card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ffb38a;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #3<\/em>, we imagine that all the players had responded to the two changes (<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span> <\/strong>and <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>) and had played cards in <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ff6700;\">dark orange<\/span><\/span><span style=\"color:#ff6700;\"> <\/span>boxes.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Team A wins, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#009e73;\">green scoreboard<\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ul>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 2<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_4E76y7AKw82EDb4\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Previous counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5&nbsp;played<strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #1)&nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_OAVahJzEB5tNrAV\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>New counterfactual game <\/strong><br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5 played&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #1&nbsp;and<br \/>\n\t\t\thad Alex&nbsp;played&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #2) <img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_ugA9tw07DzpATlX\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Tutorial - Counterfactuals \u00a0 Counterfactual games can be based on more complex scenarios. We cont...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":7,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/strong><\/u><\/p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Counterfactual games can be based on more complex scenarios. We continue with the previous example to demonstrate this.<\/p>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:1050px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"3\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 2 (continued)<\/strong>:&nbsp;We have seen that in this example&nbsp;Team A would not have won had AP-5 played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round 1&nbsp;<\/strong>(<em>the middle figure below<\/em>). However, we can also ask:<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>What would have happened had AP-5&nbsp;played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> in <\/em><em><strong>round #1<\/strong>&nbsp;and had Alex&nbsp;played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> <\/em><em>in <strong>r<\/strong><\/em><strong>ound #2<\/strong><em>?<\/em><\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><br \/>\n\t\t\tThis yields a <strong>new counterfactual <\/strong>game depicted in the <strong>right figure<\/strong> below. The differences compared to the <em>previous&nbsp;counterfactual game<\/em> in the middle&nbsp;figure are:<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #2<\/em>, we imagine that Alex had played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> instead of card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ffb38a;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #3<\/em>, we imagine that all the players had responded to the two changes (<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span> <\/strong>and <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>) and had played cards in <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ff6700;\">dark orange<\/span><\/span><span style=\"color:#ff6700;\"> <\/span>boxes.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Team A wins, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#009e73;\">green scoreboard<\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ul>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 2<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_4E76y7AKw82EDb4\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Previous counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5&nbsp;played<strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #1)&nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_OAVahJzEB5tNrAV\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>New counterfactual game <\/strong><br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5 played&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #1&nbsp;and<br \/>\n\t\t\thad Alex&nbsp;played&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #2) <img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_ugA9tw07DzpATlX\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>","DataExportTag":"Q10","QuestionID":"QID1719345409"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345410","SecondaryAttribute":"In the new counterfactual game in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #1?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In the <strong>new counterfactual game<\/strong> in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #1<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In the new counterfactual game in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #1?","Choices":{"10":{"Display":"3"},"11":{"Display":"4"},"12":{"Display":"5"},"13":{"Display":"6"},"14":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["10","11","12","13","14"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345410\/SelectableChoice\/11","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In the new counterfactual game in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #1?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">4<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345410\/SelectableChoice\/11","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345410","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345410","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":16,"NextAnswerId":1,"SubSelector":"TX","QuestionText_Unsafe":"In the <strong>new counterfactual game<\/strong> in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #1<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q11","QuestionID":"QID1719345410"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345411","SecondaryAttribute":"In\u00a0Example 2, did Alex play the same card in\u00a0round #2\u00a0of\u00a0the new counterfactual game and as in\u00a0","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In&nbsp;Example 2, did <strong>Alex<\/strong> play the same card in&nbsp;<strong>round #2<\/strong>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>the new counterfactual game<\/strong> and as in&nbsp;<strong>round #2<\/strong>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>the original game<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In\u00a0Example 2, did Alex play the same card in\u00a0round #2\u00a0of\u00a0the new counterfactual game and as in\u00a0ro...","Choices":{"7":{"Display":"Yes"},"8":{"Display":"No"}},"ChoiceOrder":["7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345411\/SelectableChoice\/8","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In&amp;nbsp;Example 2, did Alex play the same card in&amp;nbsp;round #2&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;the new counterfactual game and as in&amp;nbsp;round #2&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;the original game?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">No<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345411\/SelectableChoice\/8","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345411","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345411","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":10,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In&nbsp;Example 2, did <strong>Alex<\/strong> play the same card in&nbsp;<strong>round #2<\/strong>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>the new counterfactual game<\/strong> and as in&nbsp;<strong>round #2<\/strong>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>the original game<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q12","QuestionID":"QID1719345411"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345412","SecondaryAttribute":"Tutorial - Evaluation Task \u00a0 Now that you have understood the rules of Goofspiel and counterfactu..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Evaluation Task<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Now that you have understood the rules of Goofspiel and counterfactuals, it is time for a practice question. Your task it to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have <em><strong>low<\/strong><\/em>, <em><strong>medium<\/strong><\/em>, or <em><strong>high<\/strong><\/em> responsibility for their team losing the game.<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Consider the game in the left figure where Team A lost, and the counterfactual game in the right figure which shows what would have happened had Alex played <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">2<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round #3<\/strong>&nbsp;and had AP-5 played <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">9<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round #4<\/strong>. Once you understand what happened in the two games, <strong>please answer the question below<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Original game<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_Wik43pdVtcefyDB\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 438px;\" width=\"350\" \/>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_XImDAZ9HI0rK81X\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 438px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><br \/>\n\t\t\tRemember, while we can see all the cards, <strong>the players can&#39;t see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>.<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">To what extent do you think Alex and AP-5 are responsible for their team loosing the game? Please indicate the degree of their responsibility by selecting the appropriate choice below:<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"Matrix","Selector":"Likert","SubSelector":"SingleAnswer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","TextPosition":"inline","ChoiceColumnWidth":25,"ChoiceColumnWidthPixels":61,"RepeatHeaders":"none","WhiteSpace":"OFF","MobileFirst":true},"QuestionDescription":"Tutorial - Evaluation Task \u00a0 Now that you have understood the rules of Goofspiel and counterfactu...","Choices":{"2":{"Display":"Alex"},"3":{"Display":"AP-5"}},"ChoiceOrder":["2","3"],"Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"All"},"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":4,"Answers":{"1":{"Display":"Low Responsibility"},"2":{"Display":"Medium Responsibility"},"3":{"Display":"High Responsibility"}},"AnswerOrder":[1,"2","3"],"ChoiceDataExportTags":false,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Evaluation Task<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Now that you have understood the rules of Goofspiel and counterfactuals, it is time for a practice question. Your task it to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have <em><strong>low<\/strong><\/em>, <em><strong>medium<\/strong><\/em>, or <em><strong>high<\/strong><\/em> responsibility for their team losing the game.<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Consider the game in the left figure where Team A lost, and the counterfactual game in the right figure which shows what would have happened had Alex played <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">2<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round #3<\/strong>&nbsp;and had AP-5 played <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">9<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round #4<\/strong>. Once you understand what happened in the two games, <strong>please answer the question below<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Original game<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_Wik43pdVtcefyDB\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 438px;\" width=\"350\" \/>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_XImDAZ9HI0rK81X\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 438px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><br \/>\n\t\t\tRemember, while we can see all the cards, <strong>the players can&#39;t see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>.<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">To what extent do you think Alex and AP-5 are responsible for their team loosing the game? Please indicate the degree of their responsibility by selecting the appropriate choice below:<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q13","QuestionID":"QID1719345412"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345413","SecondaryAttribute":"Now that you have completed the tutorial, we ask you to evaluate 5 different games and report you...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: left;\">Now that you have completed the tutorial, we ask you to evaluate 5 different games and report your opinion about the players' degrees of responsibility.<\/div>\n\n<div>\n<table>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Now that you have completed the tutorial, we ask you to evaluate 5 different games and report you...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: left;\">Now that you have completed the tutorial, we ask you to evaluate 5 different games and report your opinion about the players' degrees of responsibility.<\/div>\n\n<div>\n<table>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q14","QuestionID":"QID1719345413"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345414","SecondaryAttribute":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTask Description \u00a0 In this study, you will be asked a series of questions about a te","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<u><strong>Task Description<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this study, you will be asked a series of questions about a team-based card game. Specifically, you will be asked to evaluate the <em><strong>degree of responsibility<\/strong><\/em> exhibited by each player in a team that <strong><em>lost<\/em> <\/strong>in a card game.&nbsp;<br \/>\n<br \/>\nFor this purpose, we will consider a team-based variant of the Goofspiel card game, where two teams, Team A and Team B, compete against each other. Each team consists of a human player and an AI bot.<strong><em> Alex<\/em> <em>(human)<\/em><\/strong><em> <\/em>and <strong><em>AP-5 (AI)<\/em><\/strong><em><strong> <\/strong><\/em>play in <strong><em>Team A<\/em><\/strong>, while <strong><em>Billie<\/em><\/strong> <em><strong>(human) <\/strong><\/em>and <strong><em>BB-8<\/em><\/strong> <em><strong>(AI)<\/strong><\/em> play in <strong><em>Team B<\/em><\/strong>.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nWe will first ask you to complete a <em><strong>tutorial<\/strong><\/em>. This tutorial will have three parts:<\/div>\n\n<ol>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Goofspiel<\/em>: this part explains the rules of the Goofspiel card game.<\/li>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/em>: this part explains counterfactual reasoning in Goofspiel.&nbsp;<\/li>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Evaluation Task<\/em>: this part provides an example of evaluation tasks that you will be asked to solve.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br \/>\nAfter completing the tutorial, you will be asked to evaluate 5 games. We will show you 5 Goofspiel games <em><strong>where Team A lost<\/strong><\/em>, and your task is to evaluate to what extent Alex and AP-5 are responsible for this outcome, that is, assess whether they have <strong><em>low<\/em><\/strong>, <strong><em>medium<\/em><\/strong>, or <strong><em>high<\/em><\/strong><strong> <\/strong>responsibility for Team A losing the game.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<em>Please note that all the games that you will see are illustrative examples, and they were not played by actual human-AI teams.<\/em><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"margin-left: 40px;\"><br type=\"_moz\" \/>\n&nbsp;<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTask Description \u00a0 In this study, you will be asked a series of questions about a team-based...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<u><strong>Task Description<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this study, you will be asked a series of questions about a team-based card game. Specifically, you will be asked to evaluate the <em><strong>degree of responsibility<\/strong><\/em> exhibited by each player in a team that <strong><em>lost<\/em> <\/strong>in a card game.&nbsp;<br \/>\n<br \/>\nFor this purpose, we will consider a team-based variant of the Goofspiel card game, where two teams, Team A and Team B, compete against each other. Each team consists of a human player and an AI bot.<strong><em> Alex<\/em> <em>(human)<\/em><\/strong><em> <\/em>and <strong><em>AP-5 (AI)<\/em><\/strong><em><strong> <\/strong><\/em>play in <strong><em>Team A<\/em><\/strong>, while <strong><em>Billie<\/em><\/strong> <em><strong>(human) <\/strong><\/em>and <strong><em>BB-8<\/em><\/strong> <em><strong>(AI)<\/strong><\/em> play in <strong><em>Team B<\/em><\/strong>.<br \/>\n<br \/>\nWe will first ask you to complete a <em><strong>tutorial<\/strong><\/em>. This tutorial will have three parts:<\/div>\n\n<ol>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Goofspiel<\/em>: this part explains the rules of the Goofspiel card game.<\/li>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/em>: this part explains counterfactual reasoning in Goofspiel.&nbsp;<\/li>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Evaluation Task<\/em>: this part provides an example of evaluation tasks that you will be asked to solve.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br \/>\nAfter completing the tutorial, you will be asked to evaluate 5 games. We will show you 5 Goofspiel games <em><strong>where Team A lost<\/strong><\/em>, and your task is to evaluate to what extent Alex and AP-5 are responsible for this outcome, that is, assess whether they have <strong><em>low<\/em><\/strong>, <strong><em>medium<\/em><\/strong>, or <strong><em>high<\/em><\/strong><strong> <\/strong>responsibility for Team A losing the game.<br \/>\n<br \/>\n<em>Please note that all the games that you will see are illustrative examples, and they were not played by actual human-AI teams.<\/em><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"margin-left: 40px;\"><br type=\"_moz\" \/>\n&nbsp;<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q1","QuestionID":"QID1719345414"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345415","SecondaryAttribute":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTutorial - Goofspiel \u00a0 To solve your tasks, you need to familiarize yourself with th","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<u><strong>Tutorial - Goofspiel<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">To solve your tasks, you need to familiarize yourself with the rules of the team-based version of Goofspiel. The rules are as follows:<\/div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the beginning of the game, each player receives 5 cards from the standard 52 card deck&nbsp;-&nbsp;<strong>players do not see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>, but they are aware that any given player holds cards of only one suit. Additionally, a separate deck of cards is shuffled, called <em>prize deck<\/em>.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The game proceeds in <em>rounds<\/em>. In each round, one prize card is drawn from the prize deck, and upon observing&nbsp;the prize&nbsp;card,&nbsp;the&nbsp;players simultaneously select one card from their hand. The team that plays cards with a higher sum&nbsp;wins the prize card, and the&nbsp;prize is added to the team&#39;s score. If&nbsp;the teams have equal sums, the prize card is discarded and the scores remain the same.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The game finishes after round #5, and the team with&nbsp;the highest score wins. If the teams have equal score, then it&#39;s a draw.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<div>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" height=\"630\" width=\"723\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Example 1<\/strong>: We explain how games are represented using the game below.&nbsp;The&nbsp;<em>rounds <\/em>are<em> <\/em>represented as circles: the first round (round #1) is&nbsp;on the outermost circle, while the last round (round #5)&nbsp;is on the innermost circle. The cards that players played in the game are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">grey boxes<\/span><\/span>. The prize cards are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">yellow boxes<\/span><\/span>.<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_2Bo95zy0fCWG473\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this example, all players initially received&nbsp;cards 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7 (round #1). Note that in general players do not have to receive the same cards. In the first round (round #1), <span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">prize card&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;was drawn from the prize deck,&nbsp;<\/span>both Alex and AP-5 played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/strong>, Billie played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>, and BB-8 <span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">played card <\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">.&nbsp;<\/span>Team B won the prize card&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/strong>: Team A played cards whose sum is 6, and Team B played cards whose sum is 9.<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\tTeam A won the prize cards in round #2 and round #4, achieving the score of <strong><span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><span style=\"background-color:#420516;\">11<\/span><\/span><\/strong>. Team B won all the other prizes, achieving the score of <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#420516;\">14<\/span><\/strong><\/span>. Hence, Team B won the game, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#420516;\"><strong>red scoreboard<\/strong><\/span>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><br \/>\nNow that you are familiar with the rules of Goofspiel and the game representation, we ask you to answer the questions below.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTutorial - Goofspiel \u00a0 To solve your tasks, you need to familiarize yourself with the rules...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<u><strong>Tutorial - Goofspiel<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">To solve your tasks, you need to familiarize yourself with the rules of the team-based version of Goofspiel. The rules are as follows:<\/div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the beginning of the game, each player receives 5 cards from the standard 52 card deck&nbsp;-&nbsp;<strong>players do not see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>, but they are aware that any given player holds cards of only one suit. Additionally, a separate deck of cards is shuffled, called <em>prize deck<\/em>.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The game proceeds in <em>rounds<\/em>. In each round, one prize card is drawn from the prize deck, and upon observing&nbsp;the prize&nbsp;card,&nbsp;the&nbsp;players simultaneously select one card from their hand. The team that plays cards with a higher sum&nbsp;wins the prize card, and the&nbsp;prize is added to the team&#39;s score. If&nbsp;the teams have equal sums, the prize card is discarded and the scores remain the same.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The game finishes after round #5, and the team with&nbsp;the highest score wins. If the teams have equal score, then it&#39;s a draw.&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<div>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" height=\"630\" width=\"723\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Example 1<\/strong>: We explain how games are represented using the game below.&nbsp;The&nbsp;<em>rounds <\/em>are<em> <\/em>represented as circles: the first round (round #1) is&nbsp;on the outermost circle, while the last round (round #5)&nbsp;is on the innermost circle. The cards that players played in the game are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">grey boxes<\/span><\/span>. The prize cards are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">yellow boxes<\/span><\/span>.<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_2Bo95zy0fCWG473\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this example, all players initially received&nbsp;cards 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7 (round #1). Note that in general players do not have to receive the same cards. In the first round (round #1), <span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">prize card&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;was drawn from the prize deck,&nbsp;<\/span>both Alex and AP-5 played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/strong>, Billie played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>, and BB-8 <span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">played card <\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">.&nbsp;<\/span>Team B won the prize card&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/strong>: Team A played cards whose sum is 6, and Team B played cards whose sum is 9.<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\tTeam A won the prize cards in round #2 and round #4, achieving the score of <strong><span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><span style=\"background-color:#420516;\">11<\/span><\/span><\/strong>. Team B won all the other prizes, achieving the score of <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#420516;\">14<\/span><\/strong><\/span>. Hence, Team B won the game, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#420516;\"><strong>red scoreboard<\/strong><\/span>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><br \/>\nNow that you are familiar with the rules of Goofspiel and the game representation, we ask you to answer the questions below.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/p>","DataExportTag":"Q2","QuestionID":"QID1719345415"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345416","SecondaryAttribute":"In Example 1, what card did AP-5 play in round #2?\u00a0","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In Example 1, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #2<\/strong>?&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In Example 1, what card did AP-5 play in round #2?\u00a0","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"3"},"5":{"Display":"4"},"6":{"Display":"5"},"7":{"Display":"6"},"10":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","10"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345416\/SelectableChoice\/10","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In Example 1, what card did AP-5 play in round #2?&nbsp;<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">7<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345416\/SelectableChoice\/10","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345416","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345416","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":13,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In Example 1, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #2<\/strong>?&nbsp;","DataExportTag":"Q3","QuestionID":"QID1719345416"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345417","SecondaryAttribute":"In Example 1, what was the prize in round #3?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In Example 1, what was the prize in <strong>round #3<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In Example 1, what was the prize in round #3?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"3"},"5":{"Display":"4"},"6":{"Display":"5"},"7":{"Display":"6"},"8":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345417\/SelectableChoice\/8","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In Example 1, what was the prize in round #3?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">7<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345417\/SelectableChoice\/8","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345417","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345417","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":10,"NextAnswerId":1,"SubSelector":"TX","QuestionText_Unsafe":"In Example 1, what was the prize in <strong>round #3<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q4","QuestionID":"QID1719345417"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345418","SecondaryAttribute":"In Example 1, which team won the prize in round #4?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In Example 1, which team won the prize in <strong>round #4<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In Example 1, which team won the prize in round #4?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"Team A"},"5":{"Display":"Team B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5"],"Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"All"},"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345418\/SelectableChoice\/4","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In Example 1, which team won the prize in round #4?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Team A<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345418\/SelectableChoice\/4","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345418","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345418","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":7,"NextAnswerId":5,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In Example 1, which team won the prize in <strong>round #4<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q5","QuestionID":"QID1719345418"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345419","SecondaryAttribute":"Tutorial - Counterfactuals \u00a0\u00a0 To solve your tasks, you also need to familiarize yourself with cou.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"display: block;&gt;\n\n&lt;p style=\">\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">To solve your tasks, you also need to familiarize yourself with <em>counterfactuals<\/em>.&nbsp;In this task, <em><strong>counterfactual games<\/strong><\/em> show what would have happened had the players played their cards differently. We continue with the previous example to explain counterfactual games.<\/p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 1 (continued)<\/strong>: We have seen that in this example Team A lost (<em>the left figure below<\/em>). However, consider the following question:&nbsp;<span style=\"text-align: center;\"> <\/span><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>What would have happened had AP-5 played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> in<\/em><em><strong> round #2<\/strong>?<\/em><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Clearly, nothing would have changed in <em>round #1<\/em>. However, the <strong>cards<\/strong> the players would have played in <strong>round&nbsp;#3<\/strong>, <strong>round #4<\/strong>, and <strong>round #5<\/strong>, can be <strong>different from<\/strong> those that are originally played. The <strong>right figure<\/strong> below shows the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>. The differences compared to the original game in the left figure are:<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #2<\/em>, we imagine that AP-5 had played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> instead of card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">7<\/span><\/span><\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round&nbsp;#3<\/em>, <em>round #4<\/em>, and <em>round&nbsp;#5<\/em>, we imagine that all the players had responded to this change and had played cards in<strong> <\/strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ffb38a;\">light orange<\/span><\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#d55e00;\"> <\/span><\/strong>boxes<span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><strong> <\/strong><\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Team A wins the counterfactual game, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#009e73;\">green scoreboard<\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ul>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 1&nbsp; &nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_2Bo95zy0fCWG473\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5 played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span> in round #2)<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_dV6DprmriLkQHjO\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n\n<div style=\"width: 100%; text-align: justify;\"><br \/>\nNow that you are familiar with counterfactuals games, we ask you to take a look at <em>another example<\/em>, and answer the questions below.&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 2<\/strong>: Please take a look at another game below, and one of its counterfactual games. Once you understand what happened in the counterfactual game, <strong>please answer the questions below<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 2<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_4E76y7AKw82EDb4\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had&nbsp;AP-5&nbsp;played <\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><span style=\"text-align: center;\"> in round #1)<\/span><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_OAVahJzEB5tNrAV\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Tutorial - Counterfactuals \u00a0\u00a0 To solve your tasks, you also need to familiarize yourself with cou...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"display: block;&gt;\n\n&lt;p style=\">\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">To solve your tasks, you also need to familiarize yourself with <em>counterfactuals<\/em>.&nbsp;In this task, <em><strong>counterfactual games<\/strong><\/em> show what would have happened had the players played their cards differently. We continue with the previous example to explain counterfactual games.<\/p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 1 (continued)<\/strong>: We have seen that in this example Team A lost (<em>the left figure below<\/em>). However, consider the following question:&nbsp;<span style=\"text-align: center;\"> <\/span><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>What would have happened had AP-5 played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> in<\/em><em><strong> round #2<\/strong>?<\/em><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Clearly, nothing would have changed in <em>round #1<\/em>. However, the <strong>cards<\/strong> the players would have played in <strong>round&nbsp;#3<\/strong>, <strong>round #4<\/strong>, and <strong>round #5<\/strong>, can be <strong>different from<\/strong> those that are originally played. The <strong>right figure<\/strong> below shows the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>. The differences compared to the original game in the left figure are:<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #2<\/em>, we imagine that AP-5 had played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> instead of card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">7<\/span><\/span><\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round&nbsp;#3<\/em>, <em>round #4<\/em>, and <em>round&nbsp;#5<\/em>, we imagine that all the players had responded to this change and had played cards in<strong> <\/strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ffb38a;\">light orange<\/span><\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#d55e00;\"> <\/span><\/strong>boxes<span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><strong> <\/strong><\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Team A wins the counterfactual game, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#009e73;\">green scoreboard<\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ul>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 1&nbsp; &nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_2Bo95zy0fCWG473\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5 played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span> in round #2)<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_dV6DprmriLkQHjO\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n\n<div style=\"width: 100%; text-align: justify;\"><br \/>\nNow that you are familiar with counterfactuals games, we ask you to take a look at <em>another example<\/em>, and answer the questions below.&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 2<\/strong>: Please take a look at another game below, and one of its counterfactual games. Once you understand what happened in the counterfactual game, <strong>please answer the questions below<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 2<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_4E76y7AKw82EDb4\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had&nbsp;AP-5&nbsp;played <\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><span style=\"text-align: center;\"> in round #1)<\/span><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_OAVahJzEB5tNrAV\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q6","QuestionID":"QID1719345419"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345420","SecondaryAttribute":"In the counterfactual game\u00a0in Example 2, what card did AP-5\u00a0play in round #1?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>&nbsp;in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong>&nbsp;play in <strong>round #1<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In the counterfactual game\u00a0in Example 2, what card did AP-5\u00a0play in round #1?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"3"},"5":{"Display":"4"},"6":{"Display":"5"},"7":{"Display":"6"},"8":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345420\/SelectableChoice\/5","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In the counterfactual game&amp;nbsp;in Example 2, what card did AP-5&amp;nbsp;play in round #1?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">4<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345420\/SelectableChoice\/5","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345420","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345420","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":10,"NextAnswerId":3,"SubSelector":"TX","QuestionText_Unsafe":"In the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>&nbsp;in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong>&nbsp;play in <strong>round #1<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q7","QuestionID":"QID1719345420"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345421","SecondaryAttribute":"In the counterfactual game\u00a0in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #4?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>&nbsp;in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #4<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In the counterfactual game\u00a0in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #4?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"3"},"5":{"Display":"4"},"6":{"Display":"5"},"7":{"Display":"6"},"8":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345421\/SelectableChoice\/8","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In the counterfactual game&amp;nbsp;in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #4?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">7<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345421\/SelectableChoice\/8","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345421","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345421","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":10,"NextAnswerId":3,"SubSelector":"TX","QuestionText_Unsafe":"In the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>&nbsp;in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #4<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q8","QuestionID":"QID1719345421"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345422","SecondaryAttribute":"Which team won in the counterfactual game in Example 2?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Which team won in the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong> in Example 2?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which team won in the counterfactual game in Example 2?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"Team A"},"5":{"Display":"Team B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345422\/SelectableChoice\/5","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Which team won in the counterfactual game in Example 2?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Team B<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345422\/SelectableChoice\/5","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345422","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345422","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":7,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Which team won in the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong> in Example 2?","DataExportTag":"Q9","QuestionID":"QID1719345422"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345423","SecondaryAttribute":"Tutorial - Counterfactuals \u00a0 Counterfactual games can be based on more complex scenarios. We cont..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/strong><\/u><\/p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Counterfactual games can be based on more complex scenarios. We continue with the previous example to demonstrate this.<\/p>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:1050px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"3\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 2 (continued)<\/strong>:&nbsp;We have seen that in this example&nbsp;Team A would not have won had AP-5 played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round 1&nbsp;<\/strong>(<em>the middle figure below<\/em>). However, we can also ask:<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>What would have happened had AP-5&nbsp;played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> in <\/em><em><strong>round #1<\/strong>&nbsp;and had Alex&nbsp;played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> <\/em><em>in <strong>r<\/strong><\/em><strong>ound #2<\/strong><em>?<\/em><\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><br \/>\n\t\t\tThis yields a <strong>new counterfactual <\/strong>game depicted in the <strong>right figure<\/strong> below. The differences compared to the <em>previous&nbsp;counterfactual game<\/em> in the middle&nbsp;figure are:<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #2<\/em>, we imagine that Alex had played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> instead of card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ffb38a;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #3<\/em>, we imagine that all the players had responded to the two changes (<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span> <\/strong>and <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>) and had played cards in <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ff6700;\">dark orange<\/span><\/span><span style=\"color:#ff6700;\"> <\/span>boxes.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Team A wins, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#009e73;\">green scoreboard<\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ul>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 2<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_4E76y7AKw82EDb4\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Previous counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5&nbsp;played<strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #1)&nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_OAVahJzEB5tNrAV\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>New counterfactual game <\/strong><br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5 played&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #1&nbsp;and<br \/>\n\t\t\thad Alex&nbsp;played&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #2) <img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_ugA9tw07DzpATlX\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Tutorial - Counterfactuals \u00a0 Counterfactual games can be based on more complex scenarios. We cont...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":7,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/strong><\/u><\/p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Counterfactual games can be based on more complex scenarios. We continue with the previous example to demonstrate this.<\/p>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:1050px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"3\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 2 (continued)<\/strong>:&nbsp;We have seen that in this example&nbsp;Team A would not have won had AP-5 played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round 1&nbsp;<\/strong>(<em>the middle figure below<\/em>). However, we can also ask:<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>What would have happened had AP-5&nbsp;played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> in <\/em><em><strong>round #1<\/strong>&nbsp;and had Alex&nbsp;played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> <\/em><em>in <strong>r<\/strong><\/em><strong>ound #2<\/strong><em>?<\/em><\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><br \/>\n\t\t\tThis yields a <strong>new counterfactual <\/strong>game depicted in the <strong>right figure<\/strong> below. The differences compared to the <em>previous&nbsp;counterfactual game<\/em> in the middle&nbsp;figure are:<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #2<\/em>, we imagine that Alex had played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> instead of card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ffb38a;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #3<\/em>, we imagine that all the players had responded to the two changes (<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span> <\/strong>and <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>) and had played cards in <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ff6700;\">dark orange<\/span><\/span><span style=\"color:#ff6700;\"> <\/span>boxes.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Team A wins, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#009e73;\">green scoreboard<\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ul>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 2<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_4E76y7AKw82EDb4\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Previous counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5&nbsp;played<strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #1)&nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_OAVahJzEB5tNrAV\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>New counterfactual game <\/strong><br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5 played&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #1&nbsp;and<br \/>\n\t\t\thad Alex&nbsp;played&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #2) <img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_ugA9tw07DzpATlX\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>","DataExportTag":"Q10","QuestionID":"QID1719345423"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345424","SecondaryAttribute":"In the new counterfactual game in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #1?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In the <strong>new counterfactual game<\/strong> in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #1<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In the new counterfactual game in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #1?","Choices":{"10":{"Display":"3"},"11":{"Display":"4"},"12":{"Display":"5"},"13":{"Display":"6"},"14":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["10","11","12","13","14"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345424\/SelectableChoice\/11","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In the new counterfactual game in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #1?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">4<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345424\/SelectableChoice\/11","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345424","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345424","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":16,"NextAnswerId":1,"SubSelector":"TX","QuestionText_Unsafe":"In the <strong>new counterfactual game<\/strong> in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #1<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q11","QuestionID":"QID1719345424"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345425","SecondaryAttribute":"In\u00a0Example 2, did Alex play the same card in\u00a0round #2\u00a0of\u00a0the new counterfactual game and as in\u00a0","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In&nbsp;Example 2, did <strong>Alex<\/strong> play the same card in&nbsp;<strong>round #2<\/strong>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>the new counterfactual game<\/strong> and as in&nbsp;<strong>round #2<\/strong>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>the original game<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In\u00a0Example 2, did Alex play the same card in\u00a0round #2\u00a0of\u00a0the new counterfactual game and as in\u00a0ro...","Choices":{"7":{"Display":"Yes"},"8":{"Display":"No"}},"ChoiceOrder":["7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345425\/SelectableChoice\/8","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In&amp;nbsp;Example 2, did Alex play the same card in&amp;nbsp;round #2&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;the new counterfactual game and as in&amp;nbsp;round #2&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;the original game?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">No<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345425\/SelectableChoice\/8","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345425","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345425","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":10,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In&nbsp;Example 2, did <strong>Alex<\/strong> play the same card in&nbsp;<strong>round #2<\/strong>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>the new counterfactual game<\/strong> and as in&nbsp;<strong>round #2<\/strong>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>the original game<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q12","QuestionID":"QID1719345425"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345426","SecondaryAttribute":"Tutorial - Evaluation Task \u00a0 Now that you have understood the rules of Goofspiel and counterfactu..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Evaluation Task<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Now that you have understood the rules of Goofspiel and counterfactuals, it is time for a practice question. Your task it to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have <em><strong>low<\/strong><\/em>, <em><strong>medium<\/strong><\/em>, or <em><strong>high<\/strong><\/em> responsibility for their team losing the game.<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Consider the game in the left figure where Team A lost, and the counterfactual game in the right figure which shows what would have happened had Alex played <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">2<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round #3<\/strong>&nbsp;and had AP-5 played <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">9<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round #4<\/strong>. Once you understand what happened in the two games, <strong>please answer the question below<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Original game<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_Wik43pdVtcefyDB\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 438px;\" width=\"350\" \/>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_XImDAZ9HI0rK81X\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 438px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><br \/>\n\t\t\tRemember, while we can see all the cards, <strong>the players can&#39;t see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>.<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">To what extent do you think Alex and AP-5 are responsible for their team loosing the game? Please indicate the degree of their responsibility by selecting the appropriate choice below:<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"Matrix","Selector":"Likert","SubSelector":"SingleAnswer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","TextPosition":"inline","ChoiceColumnWidth":25,"ChoiceColumnWidthPixels":61,"RepeatHeaders":"none","WhiteSpace":"OFF","MobileFirst":true},"QuestionDescription":"Tutorial - Evaluation Task \u00a0 Now that you have understood the rules of Goofspiel and counterfactu...","Choices":{"2":{"Display":"Alex"},"3":{"Display":"AP-5"}},"ChoiceOrder":["2","3"],"Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"All"},"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":5,"Answers":{"1":{"Display":"Low Responsibility"},"3":{"Display":"Medium Responsibility"},"4":{"Display":"High Responsibility"}},"AnswerOrder":["1","3","4"],"ChoiceDataExportTags":false,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Evaluation Task<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Now that you have understood the rules of Goofspiel and counterfactuals, it is time for a practice question. Your task it to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have <em><strong>low<\/strong><\/em>, <em><strong>medium<\/strong><\/em>, or <em><strong>high<\/strong><\/em> responsibility for their team losing the game.<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Consider the game in the left figure where Team A lost, and the counterfactual game in the right figure which shows what would have happened had Alex played <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">2<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round #3<\/strong>&nbsp;and had AP-5 played <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">9<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round #4<\/strong>. Once you understand what happened in the two games, <strong>please answer the question below<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Original game<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_Wik43pdVtcefyDB\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 438px;\" width=\"350\" \/>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_XImDAZ9HI0rK81X\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 438px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><br \/>\n\t\t\tRemember, while we can see all the cards, <strong>the players can&#39;t see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>.<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">To what extent do you think Alex and AP-5 are responsible for their team loosing the game? Please indicate the degree of their responsibility by selecting the appropriate choice below:<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q13","QuestionID":"QID1719345426"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345427","SecondaryAttribute":"Now that you have completed the tutorial, we ask you to evaluate 5 different games and report you...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: left;\">Now that you have completed the tutorial, we ask you to evaluate 5 different games and report your opinion about the players' degrees of responsibility.<\/div>\n\n<div>\n<table>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Now that you have completed the tutorial, we ask you to evaluate 5 different games and report you...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: left;\">Now that you have completed the tutorial, we ask you to evaluate 5 different games and report your opinion about the players' degrees of responsibility.<\/div>\n\n<div>\n<table>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q14","QuestionID":"QID1719345427"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345428","SecondaryAttribute":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b Task Description \u00a0 In this study, you will be asked a series of questions about a t","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<\/div><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><u>Task Description<\/u><\/b><\/div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this study, you will be asked a series of questions about a team-based card game. Specifically, you will be asked to evaluate the <em><strong>degree of responsibility<\/strong><\/em> exhibited by each player in a team that <strong><em>lost<\/em> <\/strong>in a card game.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\nFor this purpose, we will consider a team-based variant of the Goofspiel card game, where two teams, Team A and Team B, compete against each other. Each team consists of a human player and an AI bot.<strong><em> Alex<\/em> <em>(human)<\/em><\/strong><em> <\/em>and <strong><em>AP-5 (AI)<\/em><\/strong><em><strong> <\/strong><\/em>play in <strong><em>Team A<\/em><\/strong>, while <strong><em>Billie<\/em><\/strong> <em><strong>(human) <\/strong><\/em>and <strong><em>BB-8<\/em><\/strong> <em><strong>(AI)<\/strong><\/em> play in <strong><em>Team B<\/em><\/strong>.<br>\n<br>\nWe will first ask you to complete a <em><strong>tutorial<\/strong><\/em>. This tutorial will have three parts:<\/div>\n\n<ol>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Goofspiel<\/em>: this part explains the rules of the Goofspiel card game.<\/li>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/em>: this part explains counterfactual reasoning in Goofspiel.&nbsp;<\/li>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Evaluation Task<\/em>: this part provides an example of evaluation tasks that you will be asked to solve.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br>\nAfter completing the tutorial, you will be asked to evaluate 5 games. We will show you 5 Goofspiel games <em><strong>where Team A lost<\/strong><\/em>, and your task is to evaluate to what extent Alex and AP-5 are responsible for this outcome, that is, assess whether they have <strong><em>low<\/em><\/strong>, <strong><em>medium<\/em><\/strong>, or <strong><em>high<\/em><\/strong><strong> <\/strong>responsibility for Team A losing the game.<br>\n<br>\n<em>Please note that all the games that you will see are illustrative examples, and they were not played by actual human-AI teams.<\/em><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"margin-left: 40px;\"><br type=\"_moz\">\n&nbsp;<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b Task Description \u00a0 In this study, you will be asked a series of questions about a team-base...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<\/div><div style=\"text-align: center;\"><b><u>Task Description<\/u><\/b><\/div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this study, you will be asked a series of questions about a team-based card game. Specifically, you will be asked to evaluate the <em><strong>degree of responsibility<\/strong><\/em> exhibited by each player in a team that <strong><em>lost<\/em> <\/strong>in a card game.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\nFor this purpose, we will consider a team-based variant of the Goofspiel card game, where two teams, Team A and Team B, compete against each other. Each team consists of a human player and an AI bot.<strong><em> Alex<\/em> <em>(human)<\/em><\/strong><em> <\/em>and <strong><em>AP-5 (AI)<\/em><\/strong><em><strong> <\/strong><\/em>play in <strong><em>Team A<\/em><\/strong>, while <strong><em>Billie<\/em><\/strong> <em><strong>(human) <\/strong><\/em>and <strong><em>BB-8<\/em><\/strong> <em><strong>(AI)<\/strong><\/em> play in <strong><em>Team B<\/em><\/strong>.<br>\n<br>\nWe will first ask you to complete a <em><strong>tutorial<\/strong><\/em>. This tutorial will have three parts:<\/div>\n\n<ol>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Goofspiel<\/em>: this part explains the rules of the Goofspiel card game.<\/li>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/em>: this part explains counterfactual reasoning in Goofspiel.&nbsp;<\/li>\n <li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><em>Tutorial - Evaluation Task<\/em>: this part provides an example of evaluation tasks that you will be asked to solve.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><br>\nAfter completing the tutorial, you will be asked to evaluate 5 games. We will show you 5 Goofspiel games <em><strong>where Team A lost<\/strong><\/em>, and your task is to evaluate to what extent Alex and AP-5 are responsible for this outcome, that is, assess whether they have <strong><em>low<\/em><\/strong>, <strong><em>medium<\/em><\/strong>, or <strong><em>high<\/em><\/strong><strong> <\/strong>responsibility for Team A losing the game.<br>\n<br>\n<em>Please note that all the games that you will see are illustrative examples, and they were not played by actual human-AI teams.<\/em><\/div>\n\n<div style=\"margin-left: 40px;\"><br type=\"_moz\">\n&nbsp;<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q1","QuestionID":"QID1719345428"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345429","SecondaryAttribute":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTutorial - Goofspiel \u00a0 To solve your tasks, you need to familiarize yourself with th","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<u><strong>Tutorial - Goofspiel<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">To solve your tasks, you need to familiarize yourself with the rules of the team-based version of Goofspiel. The rules are as follows:<\/div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the beginning of the game, each player receives 5 cards from the standard 52 card deck&nbsp;-&nbsp;<strong>players do not see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>, but they are aware that any given player holds cards of only one suit. Additionally, a separate deck of cards is shuffled, called <em>prize deck<\/em>.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The game proceeds in <em>rounds<\/em>. In each round, one prize card is drawn from the prize deck, and upon observing&nbsp;the prize&nbsp;card,&nbsp;the&nbsp;players simultaneously select one card from their hand. The team that plays cards with a higher sum&nbsp;wins the prize card, and the&nbsp;prize is added to the team&#39;s score. If&nbsp;the teams have equal sums, the prize card is discarded and the scores remain the same.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The game finishes after round #5, and the team with&nbsp;the highest score wins. If the teams have equal score, then it&#39;s a draw.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<div>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" height=\"630\" width=\"723\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Example 1<\/strong>: We explain how games are represented using the game below.&nbsp;The&nbsp;<em>rounds <\/em>are<em> <\/em>represented as circles: the first round (round #1) is&nbsp;on the outermost circle, while the last round (round #5)&nbsp;is on the innermost circle. The cards that players played in the game are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">grey boxes<\/span><\/span>. The prize cards are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">yellow boxes<\/span><\/span>.<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_V09hm8sOXyz2ztT\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this example, all players initially received&nbsp;cards 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7 (round #1). Note that in general players do not have to receive the same cards. In the first round (round #1), <span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">prize card&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;was drawn from the prize deck,&nbsp;<\/span>both Alex and AP-5 played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/strong>, Billie played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>, and BB-8 <span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">played card <\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">.&nbsp;<\/span>Team B won the prize card&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/strong>: Team A played cards whose sum is 6, and Team B played cards whose sum is 9.<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\tTeam A won the prize cards in round #2 and round #4, achieving the score of <strong><span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><span style=\"background-color:#990033;\">11<\/span><\/span><\/strong>. Team B won all the other prizes, achieving the score of <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#990033;\">14<\/span><\/strong><\/span>. Hence, Team B won the game, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#990033;\"><strong>red scoreboard<\/strong><\/span>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><br \/>\nNow that you are familiar with the rules of Goofspiel and the game representation, we ask you to answer the questions below.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bTutorial - Goofspiel \u00a0 To solve your tasks, you need to familiarize yourself with the rules...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<u><strong>Tutorial - Goofspiel<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n&nbsp;\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">To solve your tasks, you need to familiarize yourself with the rules of the team-based version of Goofspiel. The rules are as follows:<\/div>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">At the beginning of the game, each player receives 5 cards from the standard 52 card deck&nbsp;-&nbsp;<strong>players do not see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>, but they are aware that any given player holds cards of only one suit. Additionally, a separate deck of cards is shuffled, called <em>prize deck<\/em>.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The game proceeds in <em>rounds<\/em>. In each round, one prize card is drawn from the prize deck, and upon observing&nbsp;the prize&nbsp;card,&nbsp;the&nbsp;players simultaneously select one card from their hand. The team that plays cards with a higher sum&nbsp;wins the prize card, and the&nbsp;prize is added to the team&#39;s score. If&nbsp;the teams have equal sums, the prize card is discarded and the scores remain the same.<\/li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The game finishes after round #5, and the team with&nbsp;the highest score wins. If the teams have equal score, then it&#39;s a draw.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n<div>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" height=\"630\" width=\"723\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td>\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Example 1<\/strong>: We explain how games are represented using the game below.&nbsp;The&nbsp;<em>rounds <\/em>are<em> <\/em>represented as circles: the first round (round #1) is&nbsp;on the outermost circle, while the last round (round #5)&nbsp;is on the innermost circle. The cards that players played in the game are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">grey boxes<\/span><\/span>. The prize cards are shown in the <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">yellow boxes<\/span><\/span>.<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_V09hm8sOXyz2ztT\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div>&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">In this example, all players initially received&nbsp;cards 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7 (round #1). Note that in general players do not have to receive the same cards. In the first round (round #1), <span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">prize card&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;was drawn from the prize deck,&nbsp;<\/span>both Alex and AP-5 played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/strong>, Billie played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>, and BB-8 <span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">played card <\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\">.&nbsp;<\/span>Team B won the prize card&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"text-size-adjust: 100%;\"><span style=\"background-color:#e6d70b;\">3<\/span><\/span><\/span><\/strong>: Team A played cards whose sum is 6, and Team B played cards whose sum is 9.<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\tTeam A won the prize cards in round #2 and round #4, achieving the score of <strong><span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><span style=\"background-color:#990033;\">11<\/span><\/span><\/strong>. Team B won all the other prizes, achieving the score of <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#990033;\">14<\/span><\/strong><\/span>. Hence, Team B won the game, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#990033;\"><strong>red scoreboard<\/strong><\/span>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><br \/>\nNow that you are familiar with the rules of Goofspiel and the game representation, we ask you to answer the questions below.&nbsp;&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/p>","DataExportTag":"Q2","QuestionID":"QID1719345429"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345430","SecondaryAttribute":"In Example 1, what card did AP-5 play in round #2?\u00a0","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In Example 1, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #2<\/strong>?&nbsp;","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In Example 1, what card did AP-5 play in round #2?\u00a0","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"3"},"5":{"Display":"4"},"6":{"Display":"5"},"7":{"Display":"6"},"10":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","10"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345430\/SelectableChoice\/10","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In Example 1, what card did AP-5 play in round #2?&nbsp;<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">7<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345430\/SelectableChoice\/10","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345430","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345430","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":13,"NextAnswerId":1,"SubSelector":"TX","QuestionText_Unsafe":"In Example 1, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #2<\/strong>?&nbsp;","DataExportTag":"Q3","QuestionID":"QID1719345430"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345431","SecondaryAttribute":"In Example 1, what was the prize in round #3?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In Example 1, what was the prize in <strong>round #3<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In Example 1, what was the prize in round #3?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"3"},"5":{"Display":"4"},"6":{"Display":"5"},"7":{"Display":"6"},"8":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345431\/SelectableChoice\/8","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In Example 1, what was the prize in round #3?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">7<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345431\/SelectableChoice\/8","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345431","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345431","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":10,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In Example 1, what was the prize in <strong>round #3<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q4","QuestionID":"QID1719345431"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345432","SecondaryAttribute":"In Example 1, which team won the prize in round #4?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In Example 1, which team won the prize in <strong>round #4<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In Example 1, which team won the prize in round #4?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"Team A"},"5":{"Display":"Team B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5"],"Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"All"},"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345432\/SelectableChoice\/4","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In Example 1, which team won the prize in round #4?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Team A<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345432\/SelectableChoice\/4","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345432","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345432","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":7,"NextAnswerId":5,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In Example 1, which team won the prize in <strong>round #4<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q5","QuestionID":"QID1719345432"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345433","SecondaryAttribute":"Tutorial - Counterfactuals \u00a0\u00a0 To solve your tasks, you also need to familiarize yourself with cou.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"display: block;&gt;\n\n&lt;p style=\">\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">To solve your tasks, you also need to familiarize yourself with <em>counterfactuals<\/em>.&nbsp;In this task, <em><strong>counterfactual games<\/strong><\/em> show what would have happened had the players played their cards differently. We continue with the previous example to explain counterfactual games.<\/p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 1 (continued)<\/strong>: We have seen that in this example Team A lost (<em>the left figure below<\/em>). However, consider the following question:&nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>What would have happened had AP-5 played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> in<\/em><em><strong> round #2<\/strong>?<\/em><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Clearly, nothing would have changed in <em>round #1<\/em>. However, the <strong>cards<\/strong> the players would have played in <strong>round&nbsp;#3<\/strong>, <strong>round #4<\/strong>, and <strong>round #5<\/strong>, can be <strong>different from<\/strong> those that are originally played. The <strong>right figure<\/strong> below shows the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>. The differences compared to the original game in the left figure are:<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #2<\/em>, we imagine that AP-5 had played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> instead of card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">7<\/span><\/span><\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round&nbsp;#3<\/em>, <em>round #4<\/em>, and <em>round&nbsp;#5<\/em>, we imagine that all the players had responded to this change and had played cards in<strong> <\/strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ffb38a;\">light orange<\/span><\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#d55e00;\"> <\/span><\/strong>boxes<span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><strong> <\/strong><\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Team A wins the counterfactual game, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#009e73;\">green scoreboard<\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ul>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 1<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; &nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_V09hm8sOXyz2ztT\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5 played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span> in round #2)<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_dV6DprmriLkQHjO\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n\n<div style=\"width: 100%; text-align: justify;\"><br \/>\nNow that you are familiar with counterfactuals games, we ask you to take a look at <em>another example<\/em>, and answer the questions below.&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 2<\/strong>: Please take a look at another game below, and one of its counterfactual games. Once you understand what happened in the counterfactual game, <strong>please answer the questions below<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 2<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_a2dMvQ2XadjTSjP\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had&nbsp;AP-5&nbsp;played <\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><span style=\"text-align: center;\"> in round #1)<\/span><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_EPbO6FaRLMnfwWn\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Tutorial - Counterfactuals \u00a0\u00a0 To solve your tasks, you also need to familiarize yourself with cou...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"display: block;&gt;\n\n&lt;p style=\">\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">To solve your tasks, you also need to familiarize yourself with <em>counterfactuals<\/em>.&nbsp;In this task, <em><strong>counterfactual games<\/strong><\/em> show what would have happened had the players played their cards differently. We continue with the previous example to explain counterfactual games.<\/p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 1 (continued)<\/strong>: We have seen that in this example Team A lost (<em>the left figure below<\/em>). However, consider the following question:&nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>What would have happened had AP-5 played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> in<\/em><em><strong> round #2<\/strong>?<\/em><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Clearly, nothing would have changed in <em>round #1<\/em>. However, the <strong>cards<\/strong> the players would have played in <strong>round&nbsp;#3<\/strong>, <strong>round #4<\/strong>, and <strong>round #5<\/strong>, can be <strong>different from<\/strong> those that are originally played. The <strong>right figure<\/strong> below shows the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>. The differences compared to the original game in the left figure are:<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #2<\/em>, we imagine that AP-5 had played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> instead of card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a6a6a6;\">7<\/span><\/span><\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round&nbsp;#3<\/em>, <em>round #4<\/em>, and <em>round&nbsp;#5<\/em>, we imagine that all the players had responded to this change and had played cards in<strong> <\/strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ffb38a;\">light orange<\/span><\/span><strong><span style=\"color:#d55e00;\"> <\/span><\/strong>boxes<span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><strong> <\/strong><\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Team A wins the counterfactual game, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#009e73;\">green scoreboard<\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ul>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 1<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; &nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_V09hm8sOXyz2ztT\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5 played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span> in round #2)<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_dV6DprmriLkQHjO\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n\n<div style=\"width: 100%; text-align: justify;\"><br \/>\nNow that you are familiar with counterfactuals games, we ask you to take a look at <em>another example<\/em>, and answer the questions below.&nbsp;<br \/>\n&nbsp;\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:875px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"2\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 2<\/strong>: Please take a look at another game below, and one of its counterfactual games. Once you understand what happened in the counterfactual game, <strong>please answer the questions below<\/strong>.<\/p>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">The original game in Example 2<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_a2dMvQ2XadjTSjP\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"text-align: center;\">Counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had&nbsp;AP-5&nbsp;played <\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><span style=\"text-align: center;\"> in round #1)<\/span><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"438\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_EPbO6FaRLMnfwWn\" style=\"height: 438px; width: 350px;\" width=\"350\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q6","QuestionID":"QID1719345433"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345434","SecondaryAttribute":"In the counterfactual game\u00a0in Example 2, what card did AP-5\u00a0play in round #1?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>&nbsp;in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong>&nbsp;play in <strong>round #1<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In the counterfactual game\u00a0in Example 2, what card did AP-5\u00a0play in round #1?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"3"},"5":{"Display":"4"},"6":{"Display":"5"},"7":{"Display":"6"},"8":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345434\/SelectableChoice\/5","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In the counterfactual game&amp;nbsp;in Example 2, what card did AP-5&amp;nbsp;play in round #1?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">4<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345434\/SelectableChoice\/5","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345434","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345434","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":9,"NextAnswerId":3,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>&nbsp;in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong>&nbsp;play in <strong>round #1<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q7","QuestionID":"QID1719345434"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345435","SecondaryAttribute":"In the counterfactual game\u00a0in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #4?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>&nbsp;in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #4<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In the counterfactual game\u00a0in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #4?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"3"},"5":{"Display":"4"},"6":{"Display":"5"},"7":{"Display":"6"},"8":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345435\/SelectableChoice\/8","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In the counterfactual game&amp;nbsp;in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #4?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">7<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345435\/SelectableChoice\/8","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345435","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345435","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":9,"NextAnswerId":3,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong>&nbsp;in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #4<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q8","QuestionID":"QID1719345435"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345436","SecondaryAttribute":"Which team won in the counterfactual game in Example 2?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Which team won in the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong> in Example 2?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"Which team won in the counterfactual game in Example 2?","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"Team A"},"5":{"Display":"Team B"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345436\/SelectableChoice\/5","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">Which team won in the counterfactual game in Example 2?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">Team B<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345436\/SelectableChoice\/5","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345436","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345436","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":7,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"Which team won in the <strong>counterfactual game<\/strong> in Example 2?","DataExportTag":"Q9","QuestionID":"QID1719345436"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345437","SecondaryAttribute":"Tutorial - Counterfactuals \u00a0 Counterfactual games can be based on more complex scenarios. We cont..","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/strong><\/u><\/p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Counterfactual games can be based on more complex scenarios. We continue with the previous example to demonstrate this.<\/p>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:1050px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"3\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 2 (continued)<\/strong>:&nbsp;We have seen that in this example&nbsp;Team A would not have won had AP-5 played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round 1&nbsp;<\/strong>(<em>the middle figure below<\/em>). However, we can also ask:<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>What would have happened had AP-5&nbsp;played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> in <\/em><em><strong>round #1<\/strong>&nbsp;and had Alex&nbsp;played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> <\/em><em>in <strong>r<\/strong><\/em><strong>ound #2<\/strong><em>?<\/em><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">This yields a <strong>new counterfactual <\/strong>game depicted in the <strong>right figure<\/strong> below. The differences compared to the <em>previous&nbsp;counterfactual game<\/em> in the middle&nbsp;figure are:<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #2<\/em>, we imagine that Alex had played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> instead of card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ffb38a;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #3<\/em>, we imagine that all the players had responded to the two changes (<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span> <\/strong>and <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>) and had played cards in <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ff6700;\">dark orange<\/span><\/span><span style=\"color:#ff6700;\"> <\/span>boxes.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Team A wins, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#009e73;\">green scoreboard<\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ul>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;The original game in Example 2<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_a2dMvQ2XadjTSjP\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Previous counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5&nbsp;played<strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #1)&nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_EPbO6FaRLMnfwWn\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>New counterfactual game <\/strong><br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5 played&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #1&nbsp;and<br \/>\n\t\t\thad Alex&nbsp;played&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #2)<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_xWDfCZrPRzqCNLl\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Tutorial - Counterfactuals \u00a0 Counterfactual games can be based on more complex scenarios. We cont...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":7,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Counterfactuals<\/strong><\/u><\/p>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">Counterfactual games can be based on more complex scenarios. We continue with the previous example to demonstrate this.<\/p>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:1050px;\">\n\t<tbody>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"3\">\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Example 2 (continued)<\/strong>:&nbsp;We have seen that in this example&nbsp;Team A would not have won had AP-5 played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> in <strong>round 1&nbsp;<\/strong>(<em>the middle figure below<\/em>). However, we can also ask:<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><em>What would have happened had AP-5&nbsp;played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> in <\/em><em><strong>round #1<\/strong>&nbsp;and had Alex&nbsp;played card <\/em><strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong><em> <\/em><em>in <strong>r<\/strong><\/em><strong>ound #2<\/strong><em>?<\/em><br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<p align=\"justify\" dir=\"ltr\">This yields a <strong>new counterfactual <\/strong>game depicted in the <strong>right figure<\/strong> below. The differences compared to the <em>previous&nbsp;counterfactual game<\/em> in the middle&nbsp;figure are:<\/p>\n\n\t\t\t<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #2<\/em>, we imagine that Alex had played card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong> instead of card <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ffb38a;\">5<\/span><\/span><\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">In <em>round #3<\/em>, we imagine that all the players had responded to the two changes (<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span> <\/strong>and <strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>) and had played cards in <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#ff6700;\">dark orange<\/span><\/span><span style=\"color:#ff6700;\"> <\/span>boxes.&nbsp;<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Team A wins, which is depicted by the <span style=\"color:#ffffff;\"><strong><span style=\"background-color:#009e73;\">green scoreboard<\/span><\/strong><\/span><span style=\"color:#000000;\">.<\/span><\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ul>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;The original game in Example 2<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_a2dMvQ2XadjTSjP\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Previous counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5&nbsp;played<strong>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #1)&nbsp;<br \/>\n\t\t\t<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_EPbO6FaRLMnfwWn\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>New counterfactual game <\/strong><br \/>\n\t\t\t(had AP-5 played&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #1&nbsp;and<br \/>\n\t\t\thad Alex&nbsp;played&nbsp;<strong><span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\">4<\/span><\/span><\/strong>&nbsp;in round #2)<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_xWDfCZrPRzqCNLl\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;<\/p>","DataExportTag":"Q10","QuestionID":"QID1719345437"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345438","SecondaryAttribute":"In the new counterfactual game in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #1?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In the <strong>new counterfactual game<\/strong> in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #1<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In the new counterfactual game in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #1?","Choices":{"10":{"Display":"3"},"11":{"Display":"4"},"12":{"Display":"5"},"13":{"Display":"6"},"14":{"Display":"7"}},"ChoiceOrder":["10","11","12","13","14"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345438\/SelectableChoice\/11","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In the new counterfactual game in Example 2, what card did AP-5 play in round #1?<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">4<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345438\/SelectableChoice\/11","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345438","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345438","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":15,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In the <strong>new counterfactual game<\/strong> in Example 2, what card did <strong>AP-5<\/strong> play in <strong>round #1<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q11","QuestionID":"QID1719345438"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345439","SecondaryAttribute":"In\u00a0Example 2, did Alex play the same card in\u00a0round #5 of\u00a0the new counterfactual game and as in\u00a0r","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"In&nbsp;Example 2, did <strong>Alex<\/strong> play the same card in&nbsp;<strong>round #5<\/strong> of&nbsp;<strong>the new counterfactual game<\/strong> and as in&nbsp;<strong>round #5<\/strong> of&nbsp;<strong>the original game<\/strong>?","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","LabelPosition":"BELOW"},"QuestionDescription":"In\u00a0Example 2, did Alex play the same card in\u00a0round #5 of\u00a0the new counterfactual game and as in\u00a0ro...","Choices":{"7":{"Display":"Yes"},"8":{"Display":"No"}},"ChoiceOrder":["7","8"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"CustomValidation","CustomValidation":{"Logic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator":"q:\/\/QID1719345439\/SelectableChoice\/8","Description":"<span class=\"ConjDesc\">If<\/span> <span class=\"QuestionDesc\">In&nbsp;Example 2, did Alex play the same card in&nbsp;round #5 of&nbsp;the new counterfactual game and as in&nbsp;ro...<\/span> <span class=\"LeftOpDesc\">No<\/span> <span class=\"OpDesc\">Is Selected<\/span> ","LeftOperand":"q:\/\/QID1719345439\/SelectableChoice\/8","LogicType":"Question","Operator":"Selected","QuestionID":"QID1719345439","QuestionIDFromLocator":"QID1719345439","QuestionIsInLoop":"no","Type":"Expression"},"Type":"If"},"Type":"BooleanExpression"},"Message":{"description":"Incorrect answer","libraryID":"UR_eFIbmxnJAeQdsIl","messageID":"MS_5AR8L0zcn4hZGWW","subMessageID":"VE_CUSTOM_VALIDATION_0"}}}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":10,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"In&nbsp;Example 2, did <strong>Alex<\/strong> play the same card in&nbsp;<strong>round #5<\/strong> of&nbsp;<strong>the new counterfactual game<\/strong> and as in&nbsp;<strong>round #5<\/strong> of&nbsp;<strong>the original game<\/strong>?","DataExportTag":"Q12","QuestionID":"QID1719345439"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345440","SecondaryAttribute":"Tutorial - Evaluation Task \u00a0\u00a0 Now that you have understood the rules of Goofspiel and counterfact.","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Evaluation Task<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Now that you have understood the rules of Goofspiel and counterfactuals, it is time for a practice question. Your task it to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have <strong><em>low<\/em><\/strong>, <strong>medium<\/strong>, or <em><strong>high<\/strong><\/em> responsibility for their team losing the game.<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:1050px;\">\n <tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n   <div>Consider the game in the <strong>middle<\/strong> figure where Team A lost, and two different counterfactual games in the figures next to it:<\/div>\n\n   <ol>\n    <li style=\"text-align: justify;\">the <strong>first <\/strong>counterfactual game shows what would have happened had Alex played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\"><strong>9<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #1<\/strong> and had Alex&nbsp;played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\"><strong>8<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #3<\/strong>.<\/li>\n    <li style=\"text-align: justify;\">the <strong>second <\/strong>counterfactual game shows what would have happened had AP-5 played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\"><strong>1<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #2&nbsp;<\/strong>and had Alex played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\"><strong>8<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #3<\/strong>.<\/li>\n   <\/ol>\n\n   <div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Once you understand what happened in the three games, <strong>please answer the question below<\/strong>.<\/div>\n   <\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align: center;\">First counterfactual game<br \/>\n   &nbsp; <img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_wYlzNNyXtHaSaMU\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n   <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Original game<br \/>\n   &nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_YaC0U1nOAGev6Bz\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n   <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Second counterfactual game<br \/>\n   &nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_ni1516rdV9amBDS\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td colspan=\"3\">\n   <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><br \/>\n   Remember, while we can see all the cards, <strong>the players can&#39;t see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\n   <div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n   <\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n <\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\"><br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">To what extent do you think Alex and AP-5 are responsible for their team loosing the game? Please indicate the degree of their responsibility by selecting the appropriate choice below:<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>","QuestionJS":false,"DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"Matrix","Selector":"Likert","SubSelector":"SingleAnswer","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","TextPosition":"inline","ChoiceColumnWidth":25,"ChoiceColumnWidthPixels":54,"RepeatHeaders":"none","WhiteSpace":"OFF","MobileFirst":true},"QuestionDescription":"Tutorial - Evaluation Task \u00a0\u00a0 Now that you have understood the rules of Goofspiel and counterfact...","Choices":{"2":{"Display":"Alex"},"3":{"Display":"AP-5"}},"ChoiceOrder":["2","3"],"Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"All"},"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":5,"NextAnswerId":5,"Answers":{"1":{"Display":"Low Responsibility"},"3":{"Display":"Medium Responsibility"},"4":{"Display":"High Responsibility"}},"AnswerOrder":["1","3","4"],"ChoiceDataExportTags":false,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: center;\">\n<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><u><strong>Tutorial - Evaluation Task<\/strong><\/u><\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div>\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Now that you have understood the rules of Goofspiel and counterfactuals, it is time for a practice question. Your task it to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have <strong><em>low<\/em><\/strong>, <strong>medium<\/strong>, or <em><strong>high<\/strong><\/em> responsibility for their team losing the game.<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"10\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width:1050px;\">\n <tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n   <div>Consider the game in the <strong>middle<\/strong> figure where Team A lost, and two different counterfactual games in the figures next to it:<\/div>\n\n   <ol>\n    <li style=\"text-align: justify;\">the <strong>first <\/strong>counterfactual game shows what would have happened had Alex played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\"><strong>9<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #1<\/strong> and had Alex&nbsp;played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\"><strong>8<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #3<\/strong>.<\/li>\n    <li style=\"text-align: justify;\">the <strong>second <\/strong>counterfactual game shows what would have happened had AP-5 played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\"><strong>1<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #2&nbsp;<\/strong>and had Alex played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\"><strong>8<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #3<\/strong>.<\/li>\n   <\/ol>\n\n   <div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Once you understand what happened in the three games, <strong>please answer the question below<\/strong>.<\/div>\n   <\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align: center;\">First counterfactual game<br \/>\n   &nbsp; <img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_wYlzNNyXtHaSaMU\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n   <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Original game<br \/>\n   &nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_YaC0U1nOAGev6Bz\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n   <td style=\"text-align: center;\">Second counterfactual game<br \/>\n   &nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_ni1516rdV9amBDS\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td colspan=\"3\">\n   <div style=\"text-align: center;\"><br \/>\n   Remember, while we can see all the cards, <strong>the players can&#39;t see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\n   <div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n   <\/td>\n  <\/tr>\n <\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\"><br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">To what extent do you think Alex and AP-5 are responsible for their team loosing the game? Please indicate the degree of their responsibility by selecting the appropriate choice below:<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q13","QuestionID":"QID1719345440"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345441","SecondaryAttribute":"Now that you have completed the tutorial, we ask you to evaluate 5 different games and report you...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<div style=\"text-align: left;\">Now that you have completed the tutorial, we ask you to evaluate 5 different games and report your opinion about the players' degrees of responsibility.<\/div>\n\n<div>\n<table>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"DB","Selector":"TB","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Now that you have completed the tutorial, we ask you to evaluate 5 different games and report you...","ChoiceOrder":[],"Validation":{"Settings":{"Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionText_Unsafe":"<div style=\"text-align: left;\">Now that you have completed the tutorial, we ask you to evaluate 5 different games and report your opinion about the players' degrees of responsibility.<\/div>\n\n<div>\n<table>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>","DataExportTag":"Q14","QuestionID":"QID1719345441"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345442","SecondaryAttribute":"The following questions are not mandatory but would be very helpful for our research. Please cons...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"The following questions are not mandatory but would be very helpful for our research. Please consider answering them!<br>\n<br>\n<br>\nWhat is your age?<br>","QuestionJS":"Qualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnload(function ()\n{\n\/\/hides the back button on a page\nthis.hidePreviousButton();\n});\n\n\nQualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnReady(function()\n{\n\t\/*Place your JavaScript here to run when the page is fully displayed*\/\n\n});\n\nQualtrics.SurveyEngine.addOnUnload(function()\n{\n\t\/*Place your JavaScript here to run when the page is unloaded*\/\n\n});","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"TE","Selector":"SL","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"The following questions are not mandatory but would be very helpful for our research. Please cons...","Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","Type":"None"}},"GradingData":[],"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":4,"NextAnswerId":1,"SearchSource":{"AllowFreeResponse":"false"},"QuestionText_Unsafe":"The following questions are not mandatory but would be very helpful for our research. Please consider answering them!<br>\n<br>\n<br>\nWhat is your age?<br>","DataExportTag":"Q1","QuestionID":"QID1719345442"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1719345443","SecondaryAttribute":"Which political party do you identify with:","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Which political party do you identify with:","DefaultChoices":false,"QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"MAVR","SubSelector":"TX","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Which political party do you identify with:","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"Democratic Party"},"5":{"Display":"Republican Party"},"6":{"Display":"Green Party"},"7":{"Display":"Libertarian Party"},"8":{"Display":"Independent"},"9":{"Display":"Other (please specify):","TextEntry":"true"}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5","6","7","8","9"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"OFF","