or:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\"><strong>3<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #1<\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ol>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Once you understand what happened in the three games, <strong>please answer the question below<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">First counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; <img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_J8pvKRa2MSy4p4b\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Original game<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_lRZAiW8HSLqhPve\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Second counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_ZfYpK8yNDshsBcS\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"3\">\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><br \/>\n\t\t\tRemember,&nbsp;<strong>the players see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\"><br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify; width: 960px;\">To what extent do you think Alex and AP-5 are responsible for their team losing the game? Please indicate the degree of their responsibility by selecting the appropriate choice below:<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>","DataExportTag":"2CF-FUL-B0-TRxCH-446","QuestionID":"QID501","QuestionType":"Matrix","Selector":"Likert","SubSelector":"SingleAnswer","QuestionDescription":"Evaluation Task \u00a0\u00a0 Your task is to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have low, medium, or high respo...","Choices":{"1":{"Displa