 left;\">\n\t\t\t<div>Consider the game in the <strong>middle<\/strong> figure where Team A lost, and two different counterfactual games in the figures next to it:<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<ol>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">the <strong>first <\/strong>counterfactual game shows what would have happened had Alex played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\"><strong>2<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #1<\/strong> and had AP-5&nbsp;played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\"><strong>2<\/strong><\/span><\/span>&nbsp;in <strong>round #1<\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">the <strong>second <\/strong>counterfactual game shows what would have happened had Alex played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\"><strong>2<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #1&nbsp;<\/strong>and had AP-5 played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\"><strong>2<\/strong><\/span><\/span>&nbsp;in <strong>round #1<\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ol>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Once you understand what happened in the three games, <strong>please answer the question below<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">First counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; <img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_zyBCuQPZhHC4Eb3\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Original game<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_mRthNG0ieAck1et\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Second counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_l4hHECToE8m7FaW\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"3\">\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><br \/>\n\t\t\tRemember,&nbsp;<strong>the players see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\"><br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify; width: 960px;\">To what extent do you think Alex and AP-5 are responsible for their team losing the game? Please indicate the degree of their responsibility by selecting the appropriate choice below:<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>","DataExportTag":"2CF-FUL-BB-HPxCH-208","QuestionID":"QID549","QuestionType":"Matrix","Selector":"Likert","SubSelector":"SingleAnswer","QuestionDescription":"Evaluation Task \u00a0\u00a0 Your task is to evaluate whether Alex and AP-5 have low, medium, or high respo...","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Alex"},"2":{"Display":"AP-5"}},"ChoiceOrder":["1","2"],"Randomization":{"Advanced":null,"TotalRandSubset":"","Type":"All"},"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"Answers":{"1":{"Display":"Low Responsibility"},"2":{"Display":"Medium Responsibility"},"3":{"Display":"High Responsibility"}},"AnswerOrder":["1","2","3"],"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText","TextPosition":"inline","RepeatHeaders":"none","WhiteSpace":"OFF","MobileFirst":true},"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":4,"ChoiceDataExportTags":false}},{"SurveyID":"SV_7PBUtX8e4Bhl1DU","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID55","SecondaryAttribute":"How confident are you in your response?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"How confident are you in your response?\n","QuestionID":"QID55","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAHR","SubSelector":"TX","QuestionDescription":"How confident are you in your response?","Choices":{"1":{"Dis