px;\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<div>Consider the game in the <strong>middle<\/strong> figure where Team A lost, and two different counterfactual games in the figures next to it:<\/div>\n\n<ol>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">the <strong>first <\/strong>counterfactual game shows what would have happened had Alex played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\"><strong>6<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #1<\/strong> and had Alex&nbsp;played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\"><strong>3<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #3<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">the <strong>second <\/strong>counterfactual game shows what would have happened had AP-5 played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\"><strong>6<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #1&nbsp;<\/strong>and had AP-5 played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#0fa65e;\"><strong>3<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #3<\/strong>.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Once you understand what happened in the three games, <strong>please answer the question below<\/strong>.<\/div>\n<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">First counterfactual game<br \/>\n&nbsp; <img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_uUaXdjQw7OpSEGq\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Original game<br \/>\n&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_oarKmIoyoUwZQSk\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Second counterfactual game<br \/>\n&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_XMZEVnfiEAq7KXV\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>