><strong>2<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #3&nbsp;<\/strong>and had AP-5 played <span style=\"color:#000000;\"><span style=\"background-color:#a8e68d;\"><strong>2<\/strong><\/span><\/span> in <strong>round #3<\/strong>.<\/li>\n\t\t\t<\/ol>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: justify;\">Once you understand what happened in the three games, <strong>please answer the question below<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">First counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp; <img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_EIaKIvpZsTnWmYN\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Original game<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_yQ5gUw6gSDUY3Bk\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">Second counterfactual game<br \/>\n\t\t\t&nbsp;<img height=\"375\" src=\"https:\/\/usc.qualtrics.com\/CP\/Graphic.php?IM=IM_7QupRmdyasHyvvV\" style=\"height: 375px; width: 300px;\" width=\"300\" \/><\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td colspan=\"3\">\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><br \/>\n\t\t\tRemember, while we can see all the cards,&nbsp;<strong>the players do not see each others&#39; cards<\/strong>.<\/div>\n\n\t\t\t<div style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;<\/div>\n\t\t\t<\/td>\n\t\t<\/tr>\n\t<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: left;\"><br \/>\n&nbsp;<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n<div style=\"text-align: justify; width: 960px;\">To what extent do you think Alex and AP-5 are responsible for their team losing the game? Please indicate the degree of their responsibility by selecting the appropriate choice below:<\/div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;<\/div>","DataExportTag":"2CF-PAR-BB-BFxCH-346","QuestionID":"QID663","QuestionType":"Matrix","Selector":"Likert","SubSelector":"SingleAnswer","QuestionD